{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBDgwqTYoCWJPdDGrRF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PLAN.md is drafted, and I'm fixing a double-bound J key, an overstated claim, and a few details a builder could trip on.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59697,"cache_read_input_tokens":334073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59697},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"49847107-8b36-41a4-8c7f-bcabf339905b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:50:31.514Z","request_id":"req_011CgjBDgcFKDovBucoHRX4U","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":2,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBDgwqTYoCWJPdDGrRF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015bfUfZkorTV1f6aMZgarbH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work && cat > .research/scratch/fix.py <<'EOF'\nimport re, sys\np = 'PLAN.md'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new, count=1):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    if n < 1 or (count and n != count):\n        sys.exit(f'expected {count} of {old!r}, found {n}')\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# Key conflict: J was both Journal and keyboard-only Skill 1; L likewise crowded. F and G are free and sit by WASD.\nrep(\"| Skill 1 (primary) | ✕ | Left click (J with no mouse) |\", \"| Skill 1 (primary) | ✕ | Left click (F with no mouse) |\")\nrep(\"| Skill 2 | □ | Right click (L with no mouse) |\", \"| Skill 2 | □ | Right click (G with no mouse) |\")\nrep(\"| Journal | Create | J (L and J only act as skills when no mouse has moved) |\", \"| Journal | Create (unbound in a session: Create + Options belongs to the hub) | J |\")\n\n# Say only what the test showed.\nrep(\"Tested: in the play preset D-pad up fires the portal and `move()` stays `[0, 0]`; in the menu preset it moves focus.\",\n    \"Tested headless: in the play preset D-pad up presses `portal` and `move()` stays `[0, 0]`; in the menu preset it presses `up` and `move()` is `[0, -1]`.\")\n\n# Tone timing must agree with the unlock rule in section 5.\nrep(\"| Tones | Level 4, with a forced prompt to the Skills screen |\", \"| Tones | Level 3, with a forced prompt to the Skills screen |\")\n\n# One weapon type for the Cantor.\nrep(\"Clapper (Ringer), Spade (Sexton), Censer or Psalter (Cantor), Crossbow (Lamplighter)\", \"Clapper (Ringer), Spade (Sexton), Psalter (Cantor), Crossbow (Lamplighter)\")\n\n# Pronouns stated for characters whose text uses them; Maud's line needs none.\nrep(\"| **Beadle Crake** | The abbey's enforcer,\", \"| **Beadle Crake** (he) | The abbey's enforcer,\")\nrep(\"On first-name terms with everyone she buries\", \"On first-name terms with everyone in the ground\")\n\n# Clearer secret-level and Greater Vigil rules.\nrep(\"Secret. Salvage a Shepherd's Bell recipe found across the Acre, Nave and March; Ysolde makes it\",\n    \"Secret. Find the three pages of a Shepherd's Bell recipe in the Acre, Nave and March; Ysolde casts it; ring it in the crater to open the way\")\nrep(\"**Greater Vigil:** after your first clear, a toggle: 5-minute timer, no deaths allowed to count toward the record; the tier reached is your score.\",\n    \"**Greater Vigil:** after your first clear, a toggle: a 5-minute timer where each death costs 10 s. Beat the timer to raise your record tier, which is your score.\")\n\n# Hub details.\nrep('content=\"Stick/WASD move, X/click attack, other buttons/RMB 1-4 skills, RS/Space roll\"', 'content=\"Stick/WASD move, ✕/click attack, □△○ R1 R2/RMB 1-4 skills, RS/Space roll\"')\nrep(\"`new E.Game({ ..., live: true, autoPause: false, menu: { quit: false, items: [] ... } })`. `autoPause: false` is essential:\",\n    \"create the game with `live: true`, `autoPause: false` and a menu with no Quit and no items of your own (the snippet is in section 17). `autoPause: false` is essential:\")\nrep(\"**Enter, ✕ or a click on Ready** call `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **△, a key the card names (M) or a click on More time** call `AIHub.answer('more')`.\",\n    \"**Enter, ✕ or a click or tap on Ready** call `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **△, a key the card names (M) or a click or tap on More time** call `AIHub.answer('more')`.\")\nrep(\"**Standings** by score, ties in one array:\", \"**Standings** list every player still in the round once, by score, with ties in one array:\")\nrep(\"- **The rule of one list:** every message handler takes a batch, so a dropped `s` costs nothing and a late `e` is applied in order.\",\n    \"- **Batches:** every handler takes a batch. A dropped `s` costs nothing because the next replaces it, and `e` is reliable, so it arrives in order.\")\n\n# Setup: fetch the protocol and the example locally so their paths are real.\nrep(\"\"\"mkdir hub && cd hub && for f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js; do\n  curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done; cd ..\"\"\",\n\"\"\"mkdir hub && cd hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do\n  curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done; cd ..\"\"\")\nrep(\"The hub's README is at `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`: read it whole; `hub/examples/arena.html` in that repo is a working shared world.\",\n    \"Read `hub/README.md` whole (the protocol); `hub/arena.html` is a working shared world.\")\n\n# The boot splash is markup in the page, before any script has run.\nrep(\"`<body>` with the boot splash (`E.bootSplash`), canvas, engine, asset set, game.\", \"`<body>` with the boot splash markup (copy it from the template's `game/index.html`), canvas, engine, asset set, game.\")\n\n# Dev mode: keep the balance export simple and usable on a pad.\nrep(\"Saved in `E.store`. Copy and paste as JSON (a text area only here).\", \"Saved in `E.store`. A Copy button puts the changed values as JSON on the clipboard and in the console, so a balance pass can become the new defaults.\")\n\n# Lighting: stay with the API card's advice.\nrep(\"Ambient about .35 in dark zones (Emberdeep's .14 is too dim for a TV across a room)\", \"Ambient about .35 to .45 in dark zones (Emberdeep's .14 is too dim for a TV across a room)\")\n\n# Testing and hygiene.\nrep(\"**Screenshots only for what a script can't check:** the look of each zone at 1920x1080,\", \"**Screenshots only for what a script can't check** (`node tools/check.mjs game/index.html --size 1920x1080`): the look of each zone,\")\nrep(\"| `hub` | Playwright, local server | The harness with `window.__hubCheck.pass` true and `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` for **all of:** `?game=F&players=2&auto=1`;\",\n    \"| `hub` | Playwright, local server | The harness with `window.__hubCheck.pass` true and `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` for **all of** these, F being your built file: `?game=F&players=2&auto=1`;\")\nrep(\"**A fast fake hub for `sim`:**\", \"**Other browsers:** smoke the final file once each in Firefox and WebKit: it loads, plays, and the TV menu scale holds.\\n\\n**A fast fake hub for `sim`:**\")\nrep(\"| 12 | **Paperwork.** About screen, exit interview, chat reply | File parses; no TODOs or stubs in the build |\",\n    \"| 12 | **Paperwork and cleanup.** About screen, exit interview, chat reply. Delete `_repo` (150 MB, and anyone can fetch it again) | File parses; no TODOs or stubs in the build |\")\n\n# American spelling throughout, as in the engine's API names.\nfor a, b in [('recoloured','recolored'),('Colour','Color'),('colours','colors'),('colour','color'),('flavour','flavor'),('Flavour','Flavor'),\n             ('stylised','stylized'),('Randomised','Randomized'),('randomised','randomized'),('neighbours','neighbors'),\n             ('centred','centered'),('centre','center'),('moulds','molds'),('mould','mold'),('Jewellery','Jewelry'),('Grey','Gray'),('grey','gray')]:\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\npython3 .research/scratch/fix.py && wc -w PLAN.md && grep -n \"GameTitle\\|exit-interview\\|claude-opus\\|20261104\\|TODO\" PLAN.md; grep -n \"[^\\x00-\\x7F]\" PLAN.md | grep -v \"✔\\|✕\\|□\\|△\\|○\\|↑\\|↓\\|←\\|→\\|♥\\|★\\|•\\|×\\|♪\\|▸\\|©\\|−\\|–\" | cut -c1-120 | head; echo '--- check for stale words'; grep -n \"J with no mouse\\|L with no mouse\\|Censer\\|Level 4, with\" PLAN.md","description":"Apply review fixes to PLAN.md and lint its wording"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"sto