{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QnNzeEwLUPqruchcyQ4rRd","type":"tool_result","content":"970 PLAN.md\n15:## 1. The game in one page\n58:## 2. Originality\n68:## 3. World and story\n70:### The world\n80:### The cast\n95:### The story\n120:### Writing style\n137:## 4. Combat\n139:### Controls\n162:### Aiming\n168:### Feel numbers (starting values, all sliders in section 15)\n175:### The strike recipe (pillar 1)\n195:### Streaks\n200:### Life and death\n209:## 5. Heroes\n220:### Bram Tolliver, the Ringer: melee bruiser\n238:### Brother Iven, the Cantor: ranged caster\n256:### Wren Ashby, the Lamplighter: ranged skirmisher\n274:### Maud Harrow, the Sexton: summoner\n296:## 6. Monsters and bosses\n325:### Elites\n345:### Bosses\n372:## 7. Loot and progression\n374:### Items\n412:### Town services\n422:### Numbers (starting values; tune with the sliders and the bot)\n447:## 8. Zones and features\n468:### The Long Vigil\n476:### Events and small things\n487:### The feature tour\n517:## 9. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n519:### Rules\n528:### Settings additions\n540:### Screens (all canvas, one panel kit, section 17)\n566:### Touch-only devices ✔\n576:## 10. Art direction\n602:## 11. Animation\n623:## 12. Audio: all in code, no files\n661:## 13. Multiplayer\n667:### World code shared by all modes\n670:### Couch co-op\n673:### AI Hub session: the round\n697:### Network design (`authority` on the host, puppets elsewhere)\n714:### Tests\n719:## 14. Attract mode\n742:## 15. Dev mode and designer tools\n744:### Dev Mode (pause menu item, hidden in sessions)\n762:### The Gallery (from Dev Mode, deep link `#gallery`)\n765:### So the rest could be built with designer tools\n775:## 16. About/Credits and the paperwork\n787:## 17. Tech plan\n789:### Setup (first half hour)\n800:### Files\n814:### Architecture rules (these prevent the expensive rewrites)\n838:### Game creation (the parts verified or that trap people)\n847:### The parts bin: Emberdeep\n865:### Engine changes to expect (you may change anything; keep a list for the feedback)\n869:### Traps\n880:## 18. Testing\n904:## 19. Order of work and cut order\n924:### Cut order\n942:## 20. Coverage checklist (TASK.md to this plan)\n| Stand still and attack | (not needed) | Hold Shift |\n| Passing Bell | D-pad ↑ | T |\n| Map | D-pad ↓ | M or Tab |\n| Inventory / Skills | D-pad ← / D-pad → | I or C / K |\n| Journal | Create (unbound in a session: Create + Options belongs to the hub) | J |\n| Pause | Options | Esc |\n| Show all loot labels | Automatic | Hold Alt |\n\nIn menus: stick or D-pad moves, ✕ confirms, ○ backs out, □ and △ are the screen's extra actions, L1 and R1 switch tabs. Keyboard: arrows, Enter, Esc. Mouse: hover moves focus, click picks, right click is the sc\n\n**Getting the D-pad free ✔:** define two input presets that differ only in where D-pad codes `Pad12`-`Pad15` go. In the play preset they are your shortcut actions, and `up down left right` have no D-pad. In the\n\n### Aiming\nAim source follows the device used last (`input.lastDevice`).\n- **Mouse:** aim at the cursor (`game.mouseGround()`). Enemies under it, found with `{ pick: unit }` and `r.pick(sx, sy)`, get an outline and their name and life at the top of the screen. Left click an enemy to\n- **Pad, or keyboard with no mouse:** assisted aim. The target is the best enemy in a 100° cone around the stick or facing direction, within the skill's range, scored by angle, distance and elite status. The he\n- **Interact target:** the nearest usable thing within 40 units gets an outline and a world prompt: `L2 Take Blessed Helm`, `E Talk`.\n\n### Feel numbers (starting values, all sliders in section 15)\n- Hero: speed 92 units/s, acceleration 1000. World scale: one tile is 16 units. Evade: .28 s at 250 units/s, i-frames for the first .22 s, 2 charges, one back every 5 s.\n- Primary skills: about 2.5 hits/s for melee, wind-up under .12 s.\n- Moving cancels the follow-through of an attack, never the strike.\n- Buffer one queued skill. Holding a skill button repeats it.\n- Enemies: shamble 28-40, rush 60-80, charge 170-190. Wind-ups: trash .25 s or more, elites .5 s or more, bosses .8 s or more. Every enemy attack telegraphs on the floor, a ground shape filling over the wind-up\n\n### The strike recipe (pillar 1)\n...\nblank lines: 195","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"b2f43f45-e81e-454e-a5ee-f45311ea3f55","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:03.965Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"970 PLAN.md\n15:## 1. The game in one page\n58:## 2. Originality\n68:## 3. World and story\n70:### The world\n80:### The cast\n95:### The story\n120:### Writing style\n137:## 4. Combat\n139:### Controls\n162:### Aiming\n168:### Feel numbers (starting values, all sliders in section 15)\n175:### The strike recipe (pillar 1)\n195:### Streaks\n200:### Life and death\n209:## 5. Heroes\n220:### Bram Tolliver, the Ringer: melee bruiser\n238:### Brother Iven, the Cantor: ranged caster\n256:### Wren Ashby, the Lamplighter: ranged skirmisher\n274:### Maud Harrow, the Sexton: summoner\n296:## 6. Monsters and bosses\n325:### Elites\n345:### Bosses\n372:## 7. Loot and progression\n374:### Items\n412:### Town services\n422:### Numbers (starting values; tune with the sliders and the bot)\n447:## 8. Zones and features\n468:### The Long Vigil\n476:### Events and small things\n487:### The feature tour\n517:## 9. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n519:### Rules\n528:### Settings additions\n540:### Screens (all canvas, one panel kit, section 17)\n566:### Touch-only devices ✔\n576:## 10. Art direction\n602:## 11. Animation\n623:## 12. Audio: all in code, no files\n661:## 13. Multiplayer\n667:### World code shared by all modes\n670:### Couch co-op\n673:### AI Hub session: the round\n697:### Network design (`authority` on the host, puppets elsewhere)\n714:### Tests\n719:## 14. Attract mode\n742:## 15. Dev mode and designer 