he brief.\nrep(\"raise `game.particles.max`, as the brief says effects are unlimited.\", \"raise `game.particles.max`.\")\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\npython3 .research/scratch/fix2.py; grep -n -i \"week\\|hour\\b\\|first half\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-140","description":"Apply second round of plan corrections"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_017UwJRNoKdwnWcwsJh8C1hb":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017UwJRNoKdwnWcwsJh8C1hb","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\n22:**Why this captures the source:** a catastrophe falling on a gothic holy town, the dead rising, mortal heroes between heaven's cold serva\n31:**The loop:** fight (seconds), loot (a minute), tune your build (minutes), ring home to town (ten minutes), chapter boss (half an hour), \n234:| Toll the Hour | 60 s | A phantom great bell falls on the target after a 1 s telegraph: 1200% in a large radius. *Toll* | **Noon:** thr\n729:2. Potter's Acre: graves erupt, Toll the Hour kills thirty. A Requiem counter.\n791:### Setup (first half hour)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"556e1350-43e2-402b-ad03-3e32a3221336","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:45.219Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok\n22:**Why this captures the source:** a catastrophe falling on a gothic holy town, the dead rising, mortal heroes between heaven's cold serva\n31:**The loop:** fight (seconds), loot (a minute), tune your build (minutes), ring home to town (ten minutes), chapter boss (half an hour), \n234:| Toll the Hour | 60 s | A phantom great bell falls on the target after a 1 s telegraph: 1200% in a large radius. *Toll* | **Noon:** thr\n729:2. Potter's Acre: graves erupt, Toll the Hour kills thirty. A Requiem counter.\n791:### Setup (first half hour)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017UwJRNoKdwnWcwsJh8C1hb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBQp4XFqACfW2xLgp1U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XCX3hBzME4pH6bM9j1Fpod","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work/PLAN.md","offset":296,"limit":222},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14877,"cache_read_input_tokens":409888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14877},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"8c05a8b4-599a-4771-83a9-71a5da4ccab7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:46.528Z","request_id":"req_011CgjBQoiS9vknTYCeNxKPt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XCX3hBzME4pH6bM9j1Fpod":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work/PLAN.md","offset":296,"limit":222}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XCX3hBzME4pH6bM9j1Fpod","type":"tool_result","content":"296\t## 6. Monsters and bosses\n297\t\n298\tEvery monster is data: body, AI kind, attacks, death style, sound. **Bodies:** `E.Humanoid` (with `build: 'skeleton'`, `hunch`, `bulky`), `E.Blob`, and custom rigs. Emberdeep's are in the repository, MIT, same owner, written to adapt: `BST_Crawler`, `BST_Serpent`, `BST_Eye` in `33-beasts.js`; recipe in `docs/CHARACTERS.md` (section 17 says how to get them).\n299\t\n300\t**AI kinds:** `shamble`, `rusher`, `charger`, `kiter`, `summoner`, `exploder`, `flier`, `burrower`, `support`. Think at about 10 Hz staggered, move every step, separate with `E.SpatialHash`, path with one `E.FlowField` aimed at every hero (`flow.update([[x, y], ...])`).\n301\t\n302\t| Monster | Where | Body and behaviour | Attack | Death |\n303\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n304\t| **Bell-Wight** | I | Hunched in rags, little bell on the wrist. Shambles, crawls out of graves. You hear the horde's bells before you see it | Claw, .35 s | Flung; its bell rolls away |\n305\t| **Bone Digger** | I | Skeleton with a spade, rusher | `overhead`, .3 s | Bursts into bones |\n306\t| **Tallow Man** | I | Bulky melting candle-man, slow, wick burning shorter | Fuse 1 s, then blast | Leaves a slowing wax pool |\n307\t| **Pall-Bearers** | I | Two skeletons carrying a coffin, one unit | Line telegraph .7 s, then charge | Coffin bursts, releasing a Wight |\n308\t| **Hushling** | I, III | Floating choirboy phantom with a sewn mouth, kiter | Slow silent note; the mix dips as it passes | Fades with a sigh |\n309\t| **Carrion Rook** | I, II | Winged Blob, swarm flier | Dive peck | Feathers |\n310\t| **The Verger** | I (elite) | Robed caster, blinks, priority target | Raises Wights from corpses | Robe collapses, empty |\n311\t| **Salt Husk** | II | Pilgrim crusted in salt, shambles | Claw | Shatters; shards fly after .3 s |\n312\t| **Brine Crawler** | II | IK-legged crab-spider, scuttles sideways | Pounce, .4 s | Legs curl |\n313\t| **Flenser** | II | Tall thin figure with paired knives | Leap slash; flees when struck | Falls apart in strips |\n314\t| **Lamprey** | II | Burrowing serpent | Ring telegraph, erupts | Thrashes |\n315\t| **Slag Effigy** | II | Bulky molten bronze, slow | Slam ring, burning pool. Armored until cooled; frost or stagger cracks it | Cools to a statue, topples |\n316\t| **Moth-Priest** | II | Robed, blinks, heals allies | Dust cone that blinds | Bursts into moths |\n317\t| **Moth swarm** | II | Tiny flock | Bites; snuffs torches | Scatters |\n318\t| **Campanar** | III | Tall, bronze mask, wings of bell-metal, glaive. Chants | Blink strike with a shield phase | Mask rings on the floor |\n319\t| **Mute** | III | Floating veiled thing | Aura: inside it only your primary works and the mix goes muffled. Sweeping beam | Unravels |\n320\t| **Clapper Hound** | III | Bronze hound | Pounce; ring on landing | Rings like a dropped pan |\n321\t| **The Unvoiced** | III | Black silhouette, seen only in light or when moving | Teleports behind you, void bomb | Gone, with no sound at all |\n322\t| **Reliquary Crab** | anywhere | Crab with a stolen reliquary on its back. Flees, spilling pennies when hit; burrows after 15 s | None | A fountain of pennies and items |\n323\t| **Lambs** | secret | Blobs in Sunday bonnets | Headbutt | Wool |\n324\t\n325\t### Elites\n326\t- **Champion pack** (blue names): 3-5 of one kind sharing 1-2 affixes. 4x life, 1.3x damage.\n327\t- **Rare** (gold name, generated: \"Sallow Penitent\", \"Brother Ash\", \"Tam the Unburied\"): 2-3 affixes, 4-6 minions. 7x life, 1.5x damage.\n328\t- Both always drop Blessed or better. Show affix names under the name.\n329\t\n330\t| Affix | What it does (always telegraphed) |\n331\t|---|---|\n332\t| Tolling | Every 6 s a ring expands from it; roll through it or be stunned |\n333\t| Waxen | Leaves slowing wax pools |\n334\t| Smoldering | Fire trail, fire on death |\n335\t| Hushed | Silence aura: only your primary works inside, sound muffled |\n336\t| Chained | Pairs linked by a burning tether |\n337\t| Mourning | Leaves a ghost that chases you 5 s |\n338\t| Cordoned | Raises a breakable ring of headstones around you |\n339\t| Shrouded | Drops frost bombs that burst after 1.5 s |\n340\t| Reverent | Pulses a shield over its allies |\n341\t| Penitent | Glows while reflecting damage; stop hitting it |\n342\t| Haunting | Teleports beside you |\n343\t| Beckoning | Pulls you to it after a telegraph |\n344\t\n345\t### Bosses\n346\tEach has a name card, phases, an arena gimmick, taunts, and a guaranteed Relic per player. Fight length target: 2 to 4 minutes on Mortal.\n347\t\n348\t**Beadle Crake (Chapter House).** Bulky rig at size 2, tricorn, long black coat, brass-topped staff, a meat hook on a chain, a ledger floating behind him. The room is an octagon with four chandeliers on rope posts and rows of pews.\n349\t- *Roll Call:* calls a hero's name, a ring fills under them (.8 s), staff slam.\n350\t- *The Hook:* line telegraph, pulls the target in, then a cleave.\n351\t- *Attendance!:* every 30 s marked pews erupt with \"absentee\" Wights. Breaking a marked pew first prevents its Wight.\n352\t- *Chandeliers:* hit a rope post when he stands under one: 12% of his life and a 3 s stun. It crushes you too.\n353\t- *Phase 2 at 50%:* \"You are marked LATE.\" Faster, charges along the aisles, cracks the floor, calls a Rare pack.\n354\t- *Death:* he is flung, the ledger bursts into pages, loot shower.\n355\t\n356\t**Regent Sallow (Moth Court).** Six braziers ring the room. Moths snuff braziers; darkness spreads from a dead brazier and hurts. Strike a brazier to relight it.\n357\t- *Phase 1:* human, in a pale gown (`heroic`, robe). Three copies; only the real one casts a shadow.\n358\t- *Phase 2 at 60%:* she unfolds into a giant moth-hag (custom rig, wings with eye spots). Gaze cone, dust clouds, diving sweeps across the room.\n359\t- *Phase 3 at 20%:* every brazier dies at once. Only heroes' own light is safe (give every hero a small lantern radius here; Wren's is bigger). A burn phase in a storm of moths.\n360\t- *Death:* \"Ask the head whose names she tore out.\"\n361\t\n362\t**The Angelus (Ringing Chamber).** A colossus at the center: bell for a head, one arm a clapper. Draw it with custom rigs or `r.queue` parts (actors cap at about 250 px tall).\n363\t- *Phase 1:* sweeping arm arcs. *The Toll:* an expanding ring you must roll through, or be stunned. Campanars join.\n364\t- *Phase 2 at 60%:* the floor breaks into four platforms joined by chains; it pulls heroes between them.\n365\t- *Phase 3 at 25%:* its bell cracks and the Hush floods in. Sound drops to almost nothing. Pockets of Hush shelter you from the Toll but drain your resource: you hide in the enemy of your enemy to survive.\n366\t- *Final blow:* at 1 life it kneels. A prompt: hold Interact to strike with the Tongue. Every local and online hero joins. Then the ending.\n367\t\n368\t**Vigil Wardens.** Composed: one of three bodies (The Pall, a floating shrouded coffin; The Cold Verger, a tall caster; The Tithe Colossus, a golem of collection plates) with patterns from one library: slam, charge, nova, summon, ring, candle rain, sweeping beam, ground spikes, blink strike, enrage. Each draws 2 close, 2 zone, 1 aid. Emberdeep's `35-bosses-core.js` and `36-bosses.js` show this.\n369\t\n370\t---\n371\t\n372\t## 7. Loot and progression\n373\t\n374\t### Items\n375\t**Slots (8):** Weapon, Head, Chest, Hands, Feet, Neck, Ring, Ring. Weapon, Head, Chest, Hands and Feet visibly change the rig (Emberdeep's `heroLook` and `dressHero` in `20-hero.js`: rebuild the rig's look when gear changes). All 1x1 in the bag; no Tetris.\n376\t**Weapons are per hero:** Clapper (Ringer), Spade (Sexton), Psalter (Cantor), Crossbow (Lamplighter). Other slots are universal. Drops roll for the finder's hero 85% of the time.\n377\t\n378\t| Rarity | Color and frame | Affixes | Notes |\n379\t|---|---|---|---|\n380\t| Worn | Gray, plain | 0 | Salvage fodder |\n381\t| Plain | White | 0-1 | |\n382\t| Blessed | Blue, rounded frame | 2 | |\n383\t| Saintly | Gold, filigree frame | 3-4 | Drops unconsecrated |\n384\t| Relic | Orange, thorned frame, name in caps | 4 + a power | Drops unconsecrated, with a **pillar of light**, a great peal and a choir swell, a star on the minimap |\n385\t| Vestment | Green, knotted frame | 4 + set bonus | Beam as Relic |\n386\t\n387\tRarity must never be told by color alone: frames and name style differ too. Quillon comments on any Relic.\n388\t\n389\t**Consecrate:** \"Unconsecrated Helm.\" Hold △ (right mouse in the bag) for 1 s. A bell swells, the name and stats arrive with a flourish. Quillon does the whole bag free in town.\n390\t\n391\t**Affix pool (about 20):** Devotion (the one main stat: +1% damage per point), Vigor (life), Armor, All Resist, Crit Chance, Crit Damage, Attack Speed, Life on Hit, Life per Second, Votive Bonus, Move Speed, Pickup Radius, Penny Find, Relic Find, Cooldown Reduction, Resource Cost Reduction, Area Damage, Candle / Shroud / Thunder / Physical %, +15% to a named skill, Socket.\n392\t\n393\t**Compare, in a line a sofa can read:** `↑ 14% Damage  ↓ 3% Toughness`, then at most 6 affix lines, then one flavor line. No tables.\n394\t\n395\t**Relics (24: 5 per hero, 4 for anyone).** Each changes how a skill plays, not just its numbers. Write them in this spirit:\n396\t- *Tongue of Saint Ossian* (Clapper): Knell also fires a ring wave.\n397\t- *The Verger's Rope* (Hands): Swing the Rope adds Ringing every second.\n398\t- *Psalter of the Drowned* (Weapon): after a Chord, Psalm fires two extra notes.\n399\t- *Blindfold of the Seventh Choir* (Head): a Chord needs only two notes.\n400\t- *The Last Wick* (Chest): Lit pools stay until you leave the zone, 3 at most.\n401\t- *Never-Dark* (Ring): your lantern's radius doubles.\n402\t- *Spade of First Soil* (Spade): Raise the Buried is free near a corpse.\n403\t- *Mother's Ring of Bones*: Corpse Burst may leave a corpse behind.\n404\t- *Ninth Bell's Shard* (Neck, anyone): every ninth hit tolls for 500%.\n405\t- *A Page of the Beadle's Ledger* (Ring, anyone): each Requiem adds Devotion for the zone.\n406\t- *A Penny for the Ferryman* (Ring, anyone): on a lethal blow, pay 1000 pennies and rise.\n407\t\n408\t**Vestment sets (4, one per hero, 4 pieces, 2-piece and 4-piece bonuses):** Vestments of the Great Rope, Habit of the Silent Choir, Watch of the Long Night, Weeds of the Potter's Field. The 4-piece makes the signature mechanic the build: Ringing stacks to 6; a Chord needs one note fewer; Lit also slows; every Buried counts as a corpse when it falls.\n409\t\n410\t**Gems:** Amber, Jet, Garnet, 3 grades. Weapon: damage / crit damage / life on hit. Armor: life / armor / resist. Jewelry: pennies / relic find / move speed.\n411\t\n412\t### Town services\n413\t| Service | Who | What |\n414\t|---|---|---|\n415\t| Forge | Ysolde | **Salvage** items into Scrap, Holy Salt, Relic Ash. **Craft:** pick a slot, pay, get a Blessed or Saintly item at your level. **Socket.** |\n416\t| Pawn | Old Penny | Sell, buy a few random items, **Blind Reliquary** (gamble pennies on an unconsecrated item of a chosen slot) |\n417\t| Chandlery | Sister Agnes | **Re-dip:** reroll one affix you choose on an item, cost rising each time |\n418\t| Stash | An iron-bound chest | 3 tabs shared by heroes in the save |\n419\t| Lantern | Mother Quillon | Consecrate all free. **Quillon's Lantern:** burn a Relic with Relic Ash, then wear its power in one of three slots (Weapon, Armor, Trinket) |\n420\t| Vigil Door | In the crater | Choose a Long Vigil tier |\n421\t\n422\t### Numbers (starting values; tune with the sliders and the bot)\n423\t- `heroWeaponDamage(L) = 8 * 1.15^(L-1)`\n424\t- `monsterLife(L) = 18 * 1.16^(L-1)`\n425\t- `monsterDamage(L) = 4 * 1.13^(L-1)`\n426\t- `heroLife(L) = 80 + 12 * L`, plus Vigor\n427\t- `xpToNext(L) = 60 * 1.35^(L-1)`\n428\t- `monsterXp(L) = 6 * 1.18^(L-1)`, x4 Champion, x8 Rare\n429\t- **Co-op per extra hero in the zone:** monster life +75%, monster damage +15%. No extra monsters.\n430\t- **Monster level:** `max(zone minimum, hero level)`, so gear is what makes you stronger, never grinding.\n431\t- **Difficulty:**\n432\t\n433\t| Level | Monster life | Monster damage | XP and loot |\n434\t|---|---|---|---|\n435\t| Mortal | x1 | x1 | +0% |\n436\t| Penitent | x2.5 | x1.7 | +25% |\n437\t| Damned | x6 | x3 | +60% |\n438\t| Anathema | x14 | x5 | +120% |\n439\t\n440\tChangeable in town after Chapter I.\n441\t\n442\t- **Pacing targets:** trash dies in 1-3 primary hits; a Rare in 15-25 s; a bot with default skills reaches about level 18 by the final boss on Mortal.\n443\t- **Verses:** after cap 30, XP buys points in four tracks: Might (damage), Flesh (life), Will (resource), Grace (speed and pickup radius).\n444\t\n445\t---\n446\t\n447\t## 8. Zones and features\n448\t\n449\tHand-laid zones are ASCII rows with a legend (`E.TileMap`). Generated zones use named layouts: `yard` (open ground, `E.gen.scatter`, prefab clearings), `halls` (rooms and corridors, `E.gen.bsp` or `rooms`, hand-written ASCII prefab rooms stitched in), `islands` (platforms over `pit` floor, bridges), `caves` (`E.gen.cave`). Emberdeep's `50-levels-core.js`, `52-layouts.js`, `51-themes.js` and `53-scenes.js` show all of it, including set dressing placed from a seeded stream.\n450\t\n451\t| # | Zone | Cells, method | Level | Look | Foes | What happens |\n452\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n453\t| 0 | **Knellwick** (hub) | ~64x64, hand | | Night rain, timber and plaster, amber windows, mud; the crater with Old Patience's roof-hole and a ring of candles | None | Services, Lychgate, stash, campfire, refugees with one-liners, a dog you can pet |\n454\t| 1 | **Potter's Acre** | ~100x100, `yard` | 1-4 | Fog, moon, dead trees, thousands of headstones with bells on strings | Wight, Digger, Rook, late Tallow | Graves erupt. Epitaphs. Event: Unquiet Row. First Lychgate. First Saintly drop guaranteed |\n455\t| 2 | **Saint Ossian's: the Nave** | ~80x60, hand | 3-6 | Marble, rose-window light on the floor, pews, candle racks, broken organ pipes | Wight, Hushling, Pall-Bearers, Verger Champions | The Beadle's roll call. Pew-smashing teaches Sacrilege. A chandelier trap taught by one easy use. Two side chapels to light |\n456\t| 3 | **The Undercroft** (2 floors) | ~70x70 each, `halls` | 5-8 | Ossuary walls, black water, candle-wax stalagmites | Digger, Tallow, Hushling, first Rare | Reliquary Crab guaranteed, Cursed Reliquary, a shrine, the set-piece crypt holding Old Patience |\n457\t| 4 | **Chapter House** | ~40x40, hand | 8 | Octagon, chandeliers | Beadle Crake | Boss. The ledger beat |\n458\t| 5 | **Saltgrave: the Audience Hall** | ~40x30, hand | | Bleached marble, moth lamps, no combat | None | The Regent, the only warm light in the game |\n459\t| 6 | **The Salt March** | ~120x90, `yard` | 8-12 | White flats under rust-red sky, sand weather, ribs of a beached bell-ship | Husk, Crawler, Flenser, Lamprey | Event: Pilgrim Caravan. A half-buried chapel as a side crypt. The contrast to Chapter I should shock |\n460\t| 7 | **The Bellworks** | ~80x80, `halls` | 11-15 | Black iron, molten bronze channels (`lava` floor), ash weather, molds big as houses | Effigy, Flenser, Moth-Priest, Rare packs | Three sluices, each a guarded fight; conveyor hazards; the pour as a scripted set piece |\n461\t| 8 | **The Moth Court** | ~44x44, hand | 15 | Pale stone, braziers | Regent Sallow | Boss. The confession |\n462\t| 9 | **The Long Stair** | ~40x160, prefab chain | 15-18 | Sky, gold cloud below, wind, the Bell rising alongside on chains | Campanar, Hound, Hushling | Five landings, each a wave fight |\n463\t| 10 | **The Scaffold of Heaven** | ~110x110, `islands` | 18-21 | Bronze platforms, chains, souls rising like embers | Campanar, Mute, Unvoiced | **The Great Toll:** every 25 s a ring sweeps the whole map; shelter in the shadow of hanging bells, or roll |\n464\t| 11 | **The Ringing Chamber** | ~56x56, hand | 22 | A bell the size of a cathedral overhead | The Angelus | Boss. Ending |\n465\t| S | **The Lambing Fields** | ~70x70, `yard` | any | Bright day, flowers, cheerful pipe music: a shock | Lambs, the Big Ewe | Secret. Find the three pages of a Shepherd's Bell recipe in the Acre, Nave and March; Ysolde casts it; ring it in the crater to open the way |\n466\t| V | **The Long Vigil** | any layout | tier | Any seen theme, recolored | All | See below |\n467\t\n468\t### The Long Vigil\n469\t- Enter by the Vigil Door. Choose a tier: tier 1 is about Penitent, each tier +17% monster life and damage, better drops.\n470\t- A random layout, theme and monster mix from a seed. No quests, just the **Reckoning** bar: trash 1%, Champion 5%, Rare 8%.\n471\t- At 100% the **Warden** arrives with a stained-glass card and its own music cue.\n472\t- Results screen: time, kills, deaths, loot, best tier per hero (a local table).\n473\t- **Pylons** appear here: Power (+100% damage), Haste, Shield, Conduit, Channel, each 20 s.\n474\t- **Greater Vigil:** after your first clear, a toggle: a 5-minute timer where each death costs 10 s. Beat the timer to raise your record tier, which is your score.\n475\t\n476\t### Events and small things\n477\t- **Unquiet Row:** graves erupt in a row; survive 40 s; a chest rises.\n478\t- **Cursed Reliquary:** a chest offers a deal; kill the count in 30 s for double loot.\n479\t- **Pilgrim Caravan:** walk a slow wagon across the March through three ambushes.\n480\t- **The Sermon:** a Moth-Priest converts pilgrims into Husks; kill it fast and fewer convert.\n481\t- **Reliquary Crab:** 1 in 3 zones, a chase.\n482\t- **Shrines:** Fervour (damage), Swiftness, Fortune (loot), Sanctuary (armor), 2 minutes, one per zone or so.\n483\t- **Lore pages:** 12, found in the world, added to the Journal, read aloud as you walk.\n484\t- **Side crypts:** a door in the Acre and the March to one small generated room set with a Rare and a chest.\n485\t- **Quillon's commentary:** non-modal lines (`talk.say(line, { auto: 2.5, modal: false })`) triggered by play. At least one in every 2 minutes of play.\n486\t\n487\t### The feature tour\n488\tThe critical path must teach and show all of this. Every row gets a one-time tip with a prompt in the player's current device.\n489\t\n490\t| Feature | First met |\n491\t|---|---|\n492\t| Move, attack, evade, potion, Votives, pennies | Prologue |\n493\t| Interact, world prompts, Quillon's chatter | Prologue |\n494\t| Item drop, compare, equip, gear changing the rig | First pack in the Prologue |\n495\t| Level up, new skill, slotting a skill | Level 2, Potter's Acre |\n496\t| Tones | Level 3, with a forced prompt to the Skills screen |\n497\t| Passing Bell, return, town services | First quest return |\n498\t| Salvage, Craft | Ysolde's quest in Knellwick |\n499\t| Consecrate | Guaranteed Saintly drop, Potter's Acre |\n500\t| Lychgates, world map | Potter's Acre |\n501\t| Events, epitaphs, lore pages | Potter's Acre |\n502\t| Sacrilege, Requiem | The Nave |\n503\t| Traps | The Nave |\n504\t| Champions, affixes | The Nave |\n505\t| Rares, shrines, Crab, Cursed Reliquary | The Undercroft |\n506\t| First boss, boss Relic | Chapter House |\n507\t| Followers | Campfire, after the Nave |\n508\t| Vows | Level 8 |\n509\t| Difficulty, the Long Vigil, Reckoning, Wardens | After Chapter I |\n510\t| Sockets, gems, Blind Reliquary, Re-dip | Chapter II, step 1 quest |\n511\t| Vestments, Quillon's Lantern | Chapter III, step 1 |\n512\t| Greater Vigil, Verses | After the first Vigil clear; cap 30 |\n513\t| Co-op | A title tip: \"Press Options on a second controller to join.\" |\n514\t\n515\t---\n516\t\n517\t## 9. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"46ade83b-0e53-4d48-ab22-6bdb42cdc4b2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:46.537Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 6. Monsters and bosses\n\nEvery monster is data: body, AI kind, attacks, death style, sound. **Bodies:** `E.Humanoid` (with `build: 'skeleton'`, `hunch`, `bulky`), `E.Blob`, and custom rigs. Emberdeep's are in the repository, MIT, same owner, written to adapt: `BST_Crawler`, `BST_Serpent`, `BST_Eye` in `33-beasts.js`; recipe in `docs/CHARACTERS.md` (section 17 says how to get them).\n\n**AI kinds:** `shamble`, `rusher`, `charger`, `kiter`, `summoner`, `exploder`, `flier`, `burrower`, `support`. Think at about 10 Hz staggered, move every step, separate with `E.SpatialHash`, path with one `E.FlowField` aimed at every hero (`flow.update([[x, y], ...])`).\n\n| Monster | Where | Body and behaviour | Attack | Death |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bell-Wight** | I | Hunched in rags, little bell on the wrist. Shambles, crawls out of graves. You hear the horde's bells before you see it | Claw, .35 s | Flung; its bell rolls away |\n| **Bone Digger** | I | Skeleton with a spade, rusher | `overhead`, .3 s | Bursts into bones |\n| **Tallow Man** | I | Bulky melting candle-man, slow, wick burning shorter | Fuse 1 s, then blast | Leaves a slowing wax pool |\n| **Pall-Bearers** | I | Two skeletons carrying a coffin, one unit | Line telegraph .7 s, then charge | Coffin bursts, releasing a Wight |\n| **Hushling** | I, III | Floating choirboy phantom with a sewn mouth, kiter | Slow silent note; the mix dips as it passes | Fades with a sigh |\n| **Carrion Rook** | I, II | Winged Blob, swarm flier | Dive peck | Feathers |\n| **The Verger** | I (elite) | Robed caster, blinks, priority target | Raises Wights from corpses | Robe collapses, empty |\n| **Salt Husk** | II | Pilgrim crusted in salt, shambles | Claw | Shatters; shards fly after .3 s |\n| **Brine Crawler** | II | IK-legged crab-spider, scuttles sideways | Pounce, .4 s | Legs curl |\n| **Flenser** | II | Tall thin figure with paired knives | Leap slash; flees when struck | Falls apart in strips |\n| **Lamprey** | II | Burrowing serpent | Ring telegraph, erupts | Thrashes |\n| **Slag Effigy** | II | Bulky molten bronze, slow | Slam ring, burning pool. Armored until cooled; frost or stagger cracks it | Cools to a statue, topples |\n| **Moth-Priest** | II | Robed, blinks, heals allies | Dust cone that blinds | Bursts into moths |\n| **Moth swarm** | II | Tiny flock | Bites; snuffs torches | Scatters |\n| **Campanar** | III | Tall, bronze mask, wings of bell-metal, glaive. Chants | Blink strike with a shield phase | Mask rings on the floor |\n| **Mute** | III | Floating veiled thing | Aura: inside it only your primary works and the mix goes muffled. Sweeping beam | Unravels |\n| **Clapper Hound** | III | Bronze hound | Pounce; ring on landing | Rings like a dropped pan |\n| **The Unvoiced** | III | Black silhouette, seen only in light or when moving | Teleports behind you, void bomb | Gone, with no sound at all |\n| **Reliquary Crab** | anywhere | Crab with a stolen reliquary on its back. Flees, spilling pennies when hit; burrows after 15 s | None | A fountain of pennies and items |\n| **Lambs** | secret | Blobs in Sunday bonnets | Headbutt | Wool |\n\n### Elites\n- **Champion pack** (blue names): 3-5 of one kind sharing 1-2 affixes. 4x life, 1.3x damage.\n- **Rare** (gold name, generated: \"Sallow Penitent\", \"Brother Ash\", \"Tam the Unburied\"): 2-3 affixes, 4-6 minions. 7x life, 1.5x damage.\n- Both always drop Blessed or better. Show affix names under the name.\n\n| Affix | What it does (always telegraphed) |\n|---|---|\n| Tolling | Every 6 s a ring expands from it; roll through it or be stunned |\n| Waxen | Leaves slowing wax pools |\n| Smoldering | Fire trail, fire on death |\n| Hushed | Silence aura: only your primary works inside, sound muffled |\n| Chained | Pairs linked by a burning tether |\n| Mourning | Leaves a ghost that chases you 5 s |\n| Cordoned | Raises a breakable ring of headstones around you |\n| Shrouded | Drops frost bombs that burst after 1.5 s |\n| Reverent | Pulses a shield over its allies |\n| Penitent | Glows while reflecting damage; stop hitting it |\n| Haunting | Teleports beside you |\n| Beckoning | Pulls you to it after a telegraph |\n\n### Bosses\nEach has a name card, phases, an arena gimmick, taunts, and a guaranteed Relic per player. Fight length target: 2 to 4 minutes on Mortal.\n\n**Beadle Crake (Chapter House).** Bulky rig at size 2, tricorn, long black coat, brass-topped staff, a meat hook on a chain, a ledger floating behind him. The room is an octagon with four chandeliers on rope posts and rows of pews.\n- *Roll Call:* calls a hero's name, a ring fills under them (.8 s), staff slam.\n- *The Hook:* line telegraph, pulls the target in, then a cleave.\n- *Attendance!:* every 30 s marked pews erupt with \"absentee\" Wights. Breaking a marked pew first prevents its Wight.\n- *Chandeliers:* hit a rope post when he stands under one: 12% of his life and a 3 s stun. It crushes you too.\n- *Phase 2 at 50%:* \"You are marked LATE.\" Faster, charges along the aisles, cracks the floor, calls a Rare pack.\n- *Death:* he is flung, the ledger bursts into pages, loot shower.\n\n**Regent Sallow (Moth Court).** Six braziers ring the room. Moths snuff braziers; darkness spreads from a dead brazier and hurts. Strike a brazier to relight it.\n- *Phase 1:* human, in a pale gown (`heroic`, robe). Three copies; only the real one casts a shadow.\n- *Phase 2 at 60%:* she unfolds into a giant moth-hag (custom rig, wings with eye spots). Gaze cone, dust clouds, diving sweeps across the room.\n- *Phase 3 at 20%:* every brazier dies at once. Only heroes' own light is safe (give every hero a small lantern radius here; Wren's is bigger). A burn phase in a storm of moths.\n- *Death:* \"Ask the head whose names she tore out.\"\n\n**The Angelus (Ringing Chamber).** A colossus at the center: bell for a head, one arm a clapper. Draw it with custom rigs or `r.queue` parts (actors cap at about 250 px tall).\n- *Phase 1:* sweeping arm arcs. *The Toll:* an expanding ring you must roll through, or be stunned. Campanars join.\n- *Phase 2 at 60%:* the floor breaks into four platforms joined by chains; it pulls heroes between them.\n- *Phase 3 at 25%:* its bell cracks and the Hush floods in. Sound drops to almost nothing. Pockets of Hush shelter you from the Toll but drain your resource: you hide in the enemy of your enemy to survive.\n- *Final blow:* at 1 life it kneels. A prompt: hold Interact to strike with the Tongue. Every local and online hero joins. Then the ending.\n\n**Vigil Wardens.** Composed: one of three bodies (The Pall, a floating shrouded coffin; The Cold Verger, a tall caster; The Tithe Colossus, a golem of collection plates) with patterns from one library: slam, charge, nova, summon, ring, candle rain, sweeping beam, ground spikes, blink strike, enrage. Each draws 2 close, 2 zone, 1 aid. Emberdeep's `35-bosses-core.js` and `36-bosses.js` show this.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Loot and progression\n\n### Items\n**Slots (8):** Weapon, Head, Chest, Hands, Feet, Neck, Ring, Ring. Weapon, Head, Chest, Hands and Feet visibly change the rig (Emberdeep's `heroLook` and `dressHero` in `20-hero.js`: rebuild the rig's look when gear changes). All 1x1 in the bag; no Tetris.\n**Weapons are per hero:** Clapper (Ringer), Spade (Sexton), Psalter (Cantor), Crossbow (Lamplighter). Other slots are universal. Drops roll for the finder's hero 85% of the time.\n\n| Rarity | Color and frame | Affixes | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Worn | Gray, plain | 0 | Salvage fodder |\n| Plain | White | 0-1 | |\n| Blessed | Blue, rounded frame | 2 | |\n| Saintly | Gold, filigree frame | 3-4 | Drops unconsecrated |\n| Relic | Orange, thorned frame, name in caps | 4 + a power | Drops unconsecrated, with a **pillar of light**, a great peal and a choir swell, a star on the minimap |\n| Vestment | Green, knotted frame | 4 + set bonus | Beam as Relic |\n\nRarity must never be told by color alone: frames and name style differ too. Quillon comments on any Relic.\n\n**Consecrate:** \"Unconsecrated Helm.\" Hold △ (right mouse in the bag) for 1 s. A bell swells, the name and stats arrive with a flourish. Quillon does the whole bag free in town.\n\n**Affix pool (about 20):** Devotion (the one main stat: +1% damage per point), Vigor (life), Armor, All Resist, Crit Chance, Crit Damage, Attack Speed, Life on Hit, Life per Second, Votive Bonus, Move Speed, Pickup Radius, Penny Find, Relic Find, Cooldown Reduction, Resource Cost Reduction, Area Damage, Candle / Shroud / Thunder / Physical %, +15% to a named skill, Socket.\n\n**Compare, in a line a sofa can read:** `↑ 14% Damage  ↓ 3% Toughness`, then at most 6 affix lines, then one flavor line. No tables.\n\n**Relics (24: 5 per hero, 4 for anyone).** Each changes how a skill plays, not just its numbers. Write them in this spirit:\n- *Tongue of Saint Ossian* (Clapper): Knell also fires a ring wave.\n- *The Verger's Rope* (Hands): Swing the Rope adds Ringing every second.\n- *Psalter of the Drowned* (Weapon): after a Chord, Psalm fires two extra notes.\n- *Blindfold of the Seventh Choir* (Head): a Chord needs only two notes.\n- *The Last Wick* (Chest): Lit pools stay until you leave the zone, 3 at most.\n- *Never-Dark* (Ring): your lantern's radius doubles.\n- *Spade of First Soil* (Spade): Raise the Buried is free near a corpse.\n- *Mother's Ring of Bones*: Corpse Burst may leave a corpse behind.\n- *Ninth Bell's Shard* (Neck, anyone): every ninth hit tolls for 500%.\n- *A Page of the Beadle's Ledger* (Ring, anyone): each Requiem adds Devotion for the zone.\n- *A Penny for the Ferryman* (Ring, anyone): on a lethal blow, pay 1000 pennies and rise.\n\n**Vestment sets (4, one per hero, 4 pieces, 2-piece and 4-piece bonuses):** Vestments of the Great Rope, Habit of the Silent Choir, Watch of the Long Night, Weeds of the Potter's Field. The 4-piece makes the signature mechanic the build: Ringing stacks to 6; a Chord needs one note fewer; Lit also slows; every Buried counts as a corpse when it falls.\n\n**Gems:** Amber, Jet, Garnet, 3 grades. Weapon: damage / crit damage / life on hit. Armor: life / armor / resist. Jewelry: pennies / relic find / move speed.\n\n### Town services\n| Service | Who | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| Forge | Ysolde | **Salvage** items into Scrap, Holy Salt, Relic Ash. **Craft:** pick a slot, pay, get a Blessed or Saintly item at your level. **Socket.** |\n| Pawn | Old Penny | Sell, buy a few random items, **Blind Reliquary** (gamble pennies on an unconsecrated item of a chosen slot) |\n| Chandlery | Sister Agnes | **Re-dip:** reroll one affix you choose on an item, cost rising each time |\n| Stash | An iron-bound chest | 3 tabs shared by heroes in the save |\n| Lantern | Mother Quillon | Consecrate all free. **Quillon's Lantern:** burn a Relic with Relic Ash, then wear its power in one of three slots (Weapon, Armor, Trinket) |\n| Vigil Door | In the crater | Choose a Long Vigil tier |\n\n### Numbers (starting values; tune with the sliders and the bot)\n- `heroWeaponDamage(L) = 8 * 1.15^(L-1)`\n- `monsterLife(L) = 18 * 1.16^(L-1)`\n- `monsterDamage(L) = 4 * 1.13^(L-1)`\n- `heroLife(L) = 80 + 12 * L`, plus Vigor\n- `xpToNext(L) = 60 * 1.35^(L-1)`\n- `monsterXp(L) = 6 * 1.18^(L-1)`, x4 Champion, x8 Rare\n- **Co-op per extra hero in the zone:** monster life +75%, monster damage +15%. No extra monsters.\n- **Monster level:** `max(zone minimum, hero level)`, so gear is what makes you stronger, never grinding.\n- **Difficulty:**\n\n| Level | Monster life | Monster damage | XP and loot |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Mortal | x1 | x1 | +0% |\n| Penitent | x2.5 | x1.7 | +25% |\n| Damned | x6 | x3 | +60% |\n| Anathema | x14 | x5 | +120% |\n\nChangeable in town after Chapter I.\n\n- **Pacing targets:** trash dies in 1-3 primary hits; a Rare in 15-25 s; a bot with default skills reaches about level 18 by the final boss on Mortal.\n- **Verses:** after cap 30, XP buys points in four tracks: Might (damage), Flesh (life), Will (resource), Grace (speed and pickup radius).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Zones and features\n\nHand-laid zones are ASCII rows with a legend (`E.TileMap`). Generated zones use named layouts: `yard` (open ground, `E.gen.scatter`, prefab clearings), `halls` (rooms and corridors, `E.gen.bsp` or `rooms`, hand-written ASCII prefab rooms stitched in), `islands` (platforms over `pit` floor, bridges), `caves` (`E.gen.cave`). Emberdeep's `50-levels-core.js`, `52-layouts.js`, `51-themes.js` and `53-scenes.js` show all of it, including set dressing placed from a seeded stream.\n\n| # | Zone | Cells, method | Level | Look | Foes | What happens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | **Knellwick** (hub) | ~64x64, hand | | Night rain, timber and plaster, amber windows, mud; the crater with Old Patience's roof-hole and a ring of candles | None | Services, Lychgate, stash, campfire, refugees with one-liners, a dog you can pet |\n| 1 | **Potter's Acre** | ~100x100, `yard` | 1-4 | Fog, moon, dead trees, thousands of headstones with bells on strings | Wight, Digger, Rook, late Tallow | Graves erupt. Epitaphs. Event: Unquiet Row. First Lychgate. First Saintly drop guaranteed |\n| 2 | **Saint Ossian's: the Nave** | ~80x60, hand | 3-6 | Marble, rose-window light on the floor, pews, candle racks, broken organ pipes | Wight, Hushling, Pall-Bearers, Verger Champions | The Beadle's roll call. Pew-smashing teaches Sacrilege. A chandelier trap taught by one easy use. Two side chapels to light |\n| 3 | **The Undercroft** (2 floors) | ~70x70 each, `halls` | 5-8 | Ossuary walls, black water, candle-wax stalagmites | Digger, Tallow, Hushling, first Rare | Reliquary Crab guaranteed, Cursed Reliquary, a shrine, the set-piece crypt holding Old Patience |\n| 4 | **Chapter House** | ~40x40, hand | 8 | Octagon, chandeliers | Beadle Crake | Boss. The ledger beat |\n| 5 | **Saltgrave: the Audience Hall** | ~40x30, hand | | Bleached marble, moth lamps, no combat | None | The Regent, the only warm light in the game |\n| 6 | **The Salt March** | ~120x90, `yard` | 8-12 | White flats under rust-red sky, sand weather, ribs of a beached bell-ship | Husk, Crawler, Flenser, Lamprey | Event: Pilgrim Caravan. A half-buried chapel as a side crypt. The contrast to Chapter I should shock |\n| 7 | **The Bellworks** | ~80x80, `halls` | 11-15 | Black iron, molten bronze channels (`lava` floor), ash weather, molds big as houses | Effigy, Flenser, Moth-Priest, Rare packs | Three sluices, each a guarded fight; conveyor hazards; the pour as a scripted set piece |\n| 8 | **The Moth Court** | ~44x44, hand | 15 | Pale stone, braziers | Regent Sallow | Boss. The confession |\n| 9 | **The Long Stair** | ~40x160, prefab chain | 15-18 | Sky, gold cloud below, wind, the Bell rising alongside on chains | Campanar, Hound, Hushling | Five landings, each a wave fight |\n| 10 | **The Scaffold of Heaven** | ~110x110, `islands` | 18-21 | Bronze platforms, chains, souls rising like embers | Campanar, Mute, Unvoiced | **The Great Toll:** every 25 s a ring sweeps the whole map; shelter in the shadow of hanging bells, or roll |\n| 11 | **The Ringing Chamber** | ~56x56, hand | 22 | A bell the size of a cathedral overhead | The Angelus | Boss. Ending |\n| S | **The Lambing Fields** | ~70x70, `yard` | any | Bright day, flowers, cheerful pipe music: a shock | Lambs, the Big Ewe | Secret. Find the three pages of a Shepherd's Bell recipe in the Acre, Nave and March; Ysolde casts it; ring it in the crater to open the way |\n| V | **The Long Vigil** | any layout | tier | Any seen theme, recolored | All | See below |\n\n### The Long Vigil\n- Enter by the Vigil Door. Choose a tier: tier 1 is about Penitent, each tier +17% monster life and damage, better drops.\n- A random layout, theme and monster mix from a seed. No quests, just the **Reckoning** bar: trash 1%, Champion 5%, Rare 8%.\n- At 100% the **Warden** arrives with a stained-glass card and its own music cue.\n- Results screen: time, kills, deaths, loot, best tier per hero (a local table).\n- **Pylons** appear here: Power (+100% damage), Haste, Shield, Conduit, Channel, each 20 s.\n- **Greater Vigil:** after your first clear, a toggle: a 5-minute timer where each death costs 10 s. Beat the timer to raise your record tier, which is your score.\n\n### Events and small things\n- **Unquiet Row:** graves erupt in a row; survive 40 s; a chest rises.\n- **Cursed Reliquary:** a chest offers a deal; kill the count in 30 s for double loot.\n- **Pilgrim Caravan:** walk a slow wagon across the March through three ambushes.\n- **The Sermon:** a Moth-Priest converts pilgrims into Husks; kill it fast and fewer convert.\n- **Reliquary Crab:** 1 in 3 zones, a chase.\n- **Shrines:** Fervour (damage), Swiftness, Fortune (loot), Sanctuary (armor), 2 minutes, one per zone or so.\n- **Lore pages:** 12, found in the world, added to the Journal, read aloud as you walk.\n- **Side crypts:** a door in the Acre and the March to one small generated room set with a Rare and a chest.\n- **Quillon's commentary:** non-modal lines (`talk.say(line, { auto: 2.5, modal: false })`) triggered by play. At least one in every 2 minutes of play.\n\n### The feature tour\nThe critical path must teach and show all of this. Every row gets a one-time tip with a prompt in the player's current device.\n\n| Feature | First met |\n|---|---|\n| Move, attack, evade, potion, Votives, pennies | Prologue |\n| Interact, world prompts, Quillon's chatter | Prologue |\n| Item drop, compare, equip, gear changing the rig | First pack in the Prologue |\n| Level up, new skill, slotting a skill | Level 2, Potter's Acre |\n| Tones | Level 3, with a forced prompt to the Skills screen |\n| Passing Bell, return, town services | First quest return |\n| Salvage, Craft | Ysolde's quest in Knellwick |\n| Consecrate | Guaranteed Saintly drop, Potter's Acre |\n| Lychgates, world map | Potter's Acre |\n| Events, epitaphs, lore pages | Potter's Acre |\n| Sacrilege, Requiem | The Nave |\n| Traps | The Nave |\n| Champions, affixes | The Nave |\n| Rares, shrines, Crab, Cursed Reliquary | The Undercroft |\n| First boss, boss Relic | Chapter House |\n| Followers | Campfire, after the Nave |\n| Vows | Level 8 |\n| Difficulty, the Long Vigil, Reckoning, Wardens | After Chapter I |\n| Sockets, gems, Blind Reliquary, Re-dip | Chapter II, step 1 quest |\n| Vestments, Quillon's Lantern | Chapter III, step 1 |\n| Greater Vigil, Verses | After the first Vigil clear; cap 30 |\n| Co-op | A title tip: \"Press Options on a second controller to join.\" |\n\n---\n\n## 9. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first","numLines":222,"startLine":296,"totalLines":973}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XCX3hBzME4pH6bM9j1Fpod","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBQp4XFqACfW2xLgp1U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VWKSw2dpzTjbiLCDWiGNkE","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work/PLAN.md","offset":721,"limit":225},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14877,"cache_read_input_tokens":409888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14877},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"2950a3d8-a6fc-44f4-be13-ebe4603df4c7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:47.959Z","request_id":"req_011CgjBQoiS9vknTYCeNxKPt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VWKSw2dpzTjbiLCDWiGNkE":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work/PLAN.md","offset":721,"limit":225}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VWKSw2dpzTjbiLCDWiGNkE","type":"tool_result","content":"721\t## 14. Attract mode\n722\t\n723\t**Trigger:** 10 seconds with no input on any front-end canvas screen (Title, Muster, Load). Not while a Settings, Controls or About screen is open; the player is reading there.\n724\t**Exit:** any input: key, mouse move or click, wheel, pad button, stick past its dead zone. Back to the title with a short fade. Use your own listener set plus a poll of `navigator.getGamepads()`, as `input.anyPressed()` doesn't see sticks or mouse moves.\n725\t**Touch-only:** it runs behind the restyled notice, and taps don't stop it (section 9).\n726\t\n727\t**What it is:** a looping tour played live by the bot, with cheats freely on (god mode, infinite resources, spawns, teleports). It uses a throwaway world and never touches saves. The director runs a list of vignettes of about 25 seconds, and the goal is to show as much of the game as possible:\n728\t1. Knellwick: the party of four walks past the services, a refugee waves, the dog is petted.\n729\t2. Potter's Acre: graves erupt, Toll the Hour kills thirty. A Requiem counter.\n730\t3. The Nave: stained-glass light, pews smashed, Champions, a chandelier trap.\n731\t4. Forced Relic drop: the beam, a pickup, a flash of the Inventory panel, the rig changing.\n732\t5. Skills panel flash: a Tone swapped, the skill recast.\n733\t6. Beadle Crake: a phase change and his death.\n734\t7. The Salt March and Bellworks, Iven's Long Note, Wren's False Dawn, Maud's Potter's Field.\n735\t8. Regent Sallow unfolding.\n736\t9. Scaffold: the Great Toll rolling past.\n737\t10. The Angelus's Toll, then the Long Vigil Reckoning filling.\n738\t11. Title splash, controls, co-op line. Loop.\n739\t\n740\tA corner overlay shows the logo and `PRESS ANY BUTTON`. Browsers won't play sound before the first gesture, so attract is silent until then. Vignettes are data in `game/src/data/attract.js`, each `{ zone, heroes, setup, seconds, script }`, so a designer can reorder them.\n741\t\n742\t---\n743\t\n744\t## 15. Dev mode and designer tools\n745\t\n746\t### Dev Mode (pause menu item, hidden in sessions)\n747\tA canvas panel with tabs, fully usable by pad, keyboard and mouse, at the same text sizes as the game. A small `DEV` marker shows while anything is on; `TUNED` while any slider differs from default.\n748\t\n749\t- **Cheats:** god mode, one-hit kills, infinite resource, no cooldowns, no-clip, freeze AI, reveal map, time scale (.1 to 3), pause and step one frame, restore life.\n750\t- **Spawn:** any monster, count, elite tier, chosen affixes; any boss, from any phase; clear enemies; any item by slot, rarity, level; Relic or set piece by name; gold, materials, levels, XP; all skills and Tones.\n751\t- **Travel:** any zone, any quest step (sets the flags), any chapter card, Vigil at tier N, the ending, the Lambing Fields, the Gallery, run the attract, autopilot on and off.\n752\t- **Balance:** the live sliders below, each applied at once, with Reset per slider, per group and all. Saved in `E.store`. A Copy button puts the changed values as JSON on the clipboard and in the console, so a balance pass can become the new defaults.\n753\t- **Overlays:** hitboxes, AI state above each monster, flow field, spawn points, network stats (RTT, messages/s, bytes), frame timing.\n754\t\n755\t**Sliders (default, range).** The most important variables, read through `TUNE.x` at the moment of use:\n756\t\n757\t| Group | Sliders |\n758\t|---|---|\n759\t| Hero | Damage x (1, .25-4), Life x (1, .25-4), Move speed x (1, .5-2), Attack speed x (1, .5-2), Cooldowns x (1, 0-2), Resource gain x (1, .25-4), Evade recharge s (5, 1-12), Potion cooldown s (20, 2-60), Votive chance (.14, 0-1) |\n760\t| Monsters | Life x (1, .25-6), Damage x (1, .25-6), Speed x (1, .5-2), Density x (1, .25-4), Elite frequency x (1, 0-4), Telegraph time x (1, .5-2), Co-op life per hero (.75, 0-2) |\n761\t| Rewards | XP x (1, 0-10), Pennies x (1, 0-10), Item drops x (1, 0-10), Relic chance x (1, 0-50), Vigil fill x (1, .25-4) |\n762\t| Feel | Hit-stop x (1, 0-3), Knockback and launch x (1, 0-3), Screen shake x (1, 0-3), Aim assist x (1, 0-2), Requiem window s (1.6, .5-4) |\n763\t\n764\t### The Gallery (from Dev Mode, deep link `#gallery`)\n765\tPlays every skill and Tone on dummies, every monster and affix walking in, attacking and dying, every boss pattern. A reel for eyes, and a test target for filmstrips and the data-coverage test.\n766\t\n767\t### So the rest could be built with designer tools\n768\tTASK.md wants the infrastructure for a full game. That means:\n769\t- **All content is data** in `game/src/data/*.js`, one registry per kind, validated by the lint. Adding a monster, skill, Relic, zone, event, quest or line needs no engine change.\n770\t- **Levels** are ASCII with a legend, generators named by data, set dressing as `[id, across, forward]` scenes.\n771\t- **Deep links:** `#zone/<id>`, `#boss/<id>/<phase>`, `#vigil/<tier>`, `#gallery/<kind>/<id>`, `#attract`, `#about`, and `?seed=`.\n772\t- **`game/CONTENT.md`,** at most two pages: how to add each kind, with one worked example. Keep it true.\n773\t- **Saves are versioned,** `game.saves` with `version` and `migrate`.\n774\t\n775\t---\n776\t\n777\t## 16. About/Credits and the paperwork\n778\t\n779\t**About/Credits screen** (title and pause, deep link `#about`): paged, L1 and R1 or arrows or a click to turn, readable at 10 feet. Contents exactly as TASK.md lists: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, and Credits: the engine (MIT, Michael Crosato), Emberdeep parts used, asset store sources by name (Kenney, KayKit and so on, each CC0), mocap sources if used, session client. Usage reads \"added on import\", as TASK.md says. \"Unknown\" for what you can't confirm.\n780\t\n781\t**One source:** keep all this in `game/src/data/about.js` and generate TASK.md's exit interview file from the same data in the build, so the screen and the file can't disagree. Check that the file parses.\n782\t\n783\t**Exit interview's `aiHub` block, suggested:** type `Game`, genre `RPG`, source `Diablo 3`, series `Diablo`, players `1–4`, tags from `co-op`, `fantasy`, `pixel art`, `boss fights`, `story`, plus `isometric`. Controls in one line. Tagline and description in the game's voice, without the source's names.\n784\t\n785\tRemember the chat reply too: TASK.md requires the same information there.\n786\t\n787\t---\n788\t\n789\t## 17. Tech plan\n790\t\n791\t### Setup (first half hour)\n792\t```sh\n793\t# in your dev folder\n794\tgit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge _repo     # for Emberdeep parts, mocap; never bundled whole\n795\tcp -r _repo/dist/handoff/. .                                              # the handoff: its layout is the dev folder's layout\n796\tnpm install                                                               # Playwright 1.63.0. Never `playwright install` here\n797\tmkdir hub && cd hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do\n798\t  curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done; cd ..\n799\t```\n800\tRead `API.md` whole, then `docs/ASSETS.md`, and search `API-INDEX.md` and `AI_GUIDE.md` for names. Read `hub/README.md` whole (the protocol); `hub/arena.html` is a working shared world. Stack: plain JavaScript on the full engine (`my-3d2dge.js`, all modules included). No other libraries, no CDN needed.\n801\t\n802\t### Files\n803\t```\n804\tmy-3d2dge.js, API.md, tools/, kits/, ...   the handoff\n805\tgame/index.html                            dev page (loads the built game.js)\n806\tgame/src/00-core.js ... 90-start.js        joined in name order into one IIFE (Emberdeep's pattern)\n807\tgame/src/data/*.js                         all content\n808\tgame/CONTENT.md                            designer's how-to\n809\ttools/build.mjs                            join; inline session.js, engine, asset set, game into the single HTML\n810\ttools/test.mjs                             the one test command (section 18)\n811\t```\n812\tSuggested parts of `game/src`: `core` (game, `def`, BUS, RNG streams, TUNE), `input` (presets, prompts, aim), `world` (world, step), `combat` (damage, statuses, fx verbs), `hero`, `skills`, `ai` (monsters, bot), `loot`, `progress` (XP, Vows, quests, saves), `render-*` (rigs, gear, themes, props, decals, fx, lights), `ui-*` (panel kit, HUD, each screen), `net`, `audio-*` (synth, music, sfx, voice), `attract`, `dev`, `about`.\n813\t\n814\t**The single file:** `<meta charset>`, then `session.js` as the first script, unmodified; hub tags; `<title>`; styles; `<body>` with the boot splash markup (copy it from the template's `game/index.html`), canvas, engine, asset set, game. Write every `</script` inside inlined scripts as `<\\/script`. It must run from `file://` with no network.\n815\t\n816\t### Architecture rules (these prevent the expensive rewrites)\n817\t1. **`world` holds everything; no hero singleton.** `world.heroes[]`, `world.me` (null on a server copy), `world.foes`, `world.fx`, `world.drops`, `world.map`, `world.authority`.\n818\t2. **Heroes read an abstract input,** `{ moveDir, aim, pressed(slot), ... }`, built from a device (`game.players[i]`), the bot, or the network. Nothing in hero code touches `game.input`.\n819\t3. **The simulation never reads rigs or draws.** Visuals read the sim. Spawn projectiles from fixed offsets and let the visual start at the hand. So a server copy and headless runs can skip rig updates entirely.\n820\t4. **One damage pipeline:** `dealDamage(target, hit)`, only when `world.authority`.\n821\t5. **Every effect is a verb with JSON params:** `fx('cone' | 'bolt' | 'nova' | 'area' | 'telegraph' | 'chain' | 'beam' | 'wave' | 'pull' | 'leap' | 'summon' | 'lob', params)`. Skills, monsters, bosses, traps and Relics all use them. See `FX.*` in Emberdeep's `10-combat.js`.\n822\t6. **Randomness from named streams** (`E.rng(seed)`; in a session `AIHub.rng(label)`): `map`, `loot`, `ai`, cosmetics apart. `Math.random` never affects the sim: in shared world it isn't seeded, and rigs call it for blinks.\n823\t7. **All content through `def(kind, id, spec)`,** referred to by id. Listeners on a `BUS` (`hit`, `kill`, `skill`, `evade`, `pickup`, `step`) let Relics and tips attach without touching combat.\n824\t8. **Knobs:** every balance number reads `TUNE.x` when used.\n825\t9. **UI layouts and rects are computed in `update`,** drawn in `draw`, so mouse hits and tests work headless. Input is read only in `update`.\n826\t10. **One panel kit:** focusable rects with automatic directional navigation (nearest rect in the pressed direction), `input.repeat`, hover sets focus, click picks, a prompt bar at the bottom that follows the last device.\n827\t\n828\t**Data shapes, to set the pattern:**\n829\t```js\n830\tdef('skill', 'knell', { hero: 'ringer', name: 'Knell', unlock: 3, cost: { peal: 30 }, cd: 0, icon: 'bellSlam', tags: ['toll'],\n831\t  move: 'overhead', wind: .22, active: .1, recover: .3,\n832\t  verbs: [{ fx: 'cone', on: 'active', range: 40, half: .9, dmg: 3.2, el: 'phys', kb: 120 }],\n833\t  tones: { deep: { name: 'Deep', text: 'A ring drags foes in before it lands.', add: [{ fx: 'pull', on: 'wind', r: 70, power: 140 }] } /* ... */ } });\n834\tdef('monster', 'bellWight', { name: 'Bell-Wight', body: { rig: 'humanoid', o: { hunch: .35, size: 1.15, outfit: 'tunic' } }, ai: 'shamble', speed: 32,\n835\t  life: 1, dmg: 1, xp: 1, attacks: [{ move: 'claw', wind: .35, range: 14, dmg: 1 }], enter: 'graveRise', death: 'fling', sound: { idle: 'smallBell' }, tags: ['undead'] });\n836\tdef('zone', 'pottersAcre', { name: \"Potter's Acre\", chapter: 1, level: [1, 4], layout: 'yard', size: [100, 100], theme: 'graveyard',\n837\t  pool: { bellWight: 10, boneDigger: 4, carrionRook: 2 }, elites: [1, 2], events: ['unquietRow'], shrines: 1, music: 'acre', weather: { kind: 'rain', amount: .4 }, lychgate: true });\n838\t```\n839\t\n840\t### Game creation (the parts verified or that trap people)\n841\t```js\n842\tconst session = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\n843\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [480, 270], expand: true, view: 'iso', bg: '#05040a', touch: 'never',\n844\t  input: PLAY_PRESET, live: session, autoPause: !session,\n845\t  menu: { items: session ? [] : PAUSE_ITEMS, quit: session ? false : 'title', controls: CONTROL_NAMES,\n846\t    settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox (A B X Y)']] }, /* yours */] } });\n847\t```\n848\t\n849\t### The parts bin: Emberdeep\n850\t`_repo/src/emberdeep/` is a whole Diablo-style game on this engine, MIT, same owner. **Do not fork it.** It assumes one hero (`ED.hero` appears 354 times ✔), its menus are mouse-first and replace the standard ones, its UI is small and dense, and it's a different game. Instead, read `DESIGN.md`, copy algorithms and rigs out, rename everything to this game's terms, and credit it.\n851\t\n852\t| You need | Look at |\n853\t|---|---|\n854\t| Damage, knockback, FX verbs | `10-combat.js`, `05-elements.js` |\n855\t| Hero actions, roll, IK potion, wounded hunch, gear look | `20-hero.js` |\n856\t| Skill runtime and worked skills | `25-skills-core.js`, `26-skills-melee.js`, `27-skills-spells.js` |\n857\t| Monster AI, affixes, worked monsters | `30-monsters-core.js`, `31-monsters.js` |\n858\t| Crawler, serpent, eye rigs | `33-beasts.js` |\n859\t| Boss runtime and pattern library | `35-bosses-core.js`, `36-bosses.js` |\n860\t| Item generation, labels, panels | `40-loot-core.js`, `42-inventory.js` |\n861\t| Level building, floors, themes, dressing | `50-levels-core.js`, `51-themes.js`, `52-layouts.js`, `53-scenes.js` |\n862\t| NPCs and a town | `55-town-core.js`, `56-town.js` |\n863\t| Dev tools, tuning, gallery, autopilot, rumble | `62-developer.js`, `01-tune.js`, `92-gallery.js`, `93-autopilot.js`, `97-rumble.js` |\n864\t\n865\t**`kits/adventure.js`** is the kit the API card names for this genre: read how it sets scenes, lights and GPU fallback. `kits/brawler.js` shows drop-in players. `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs` show the Node stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`). Then start from the rules above rather than bending a kit.\n866\t\n867\t### Engine changes to expect (you may change anything; keep a list for the feedback)\n868\t- **Weapons and hats are closed lists** ✔ (constructor at about line 4073, `['sword', 'gun', 'staff']`; drawing at about lines 4649-4656 and 4729-4736). Add a registry: `E.Humanoid.WEAPONS[id] = { len, draw(g, ctx) }`, accept those ids, draw them there, set `bladeLen`. A dozen builders did the same. Same for hats, plus a draw hook for attachments (rope wraps, blindfold, mask, wings).\n869\t- **Pan and loops** on sound aren't built in: your own synth handles them.\n870\t\n871\t### Traps\n872\t- `game.go` clears timers, tweens, particles and weather (`{ keep: true }` outlives it). Tests set `game.fadeTime = 0`.\n873\t- A frame past 50 ms gives up its time. A browser test waits on state, never the clock.\n874\t- `E.font` text with characters it lacks prints `?`. Colors must be `#rrggbb`; a bad one draws magenta.\n875\t- `input.tap` is no device, so prompts don't change in tests. `input.feed('move', x, y)` plays a pointer.\n876\t- `r.pick` needs a drawn frame: hover tests need the browser or `draw: true`.\n877\t- A map over 128x128 bakes floors in chunks automatically.\n878\t- Weather ends with the scene: set it in `enter`.\n879\t\n880\t---\n881\t\n882\t## 18. Testing\n883\t\n884\t**One command:** `node tools/test.mjs [data|sim|play|browser|hub]` (no argument: all). It prints only failures and a final one-line count. Rerun a suite only after changing what it covers. Don't use subagents or workflows to review, debate or judge. Use the stand-ins TASK.md lists: a `navigator.getGamepads` stub with a standard-mapping pad, Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, `OfflineAudioContext` and `AnalyserNode`, two browser pages for multiplayer. One or two browsers at a time, closed when done. No server unless needed; when needed, `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page is yours, stop your own PID only.\n885\t\n886\t| Suite | Runs in | Checks |\n887\t|---|---|---|\n888\t| `data` | Node | Every registry's required fields; every referenced id exists; every skill has 3 Tones with text; 24 Relics; every string uses only font characters and fits its box (`E.font.width`); the banned-word list; every quest step's target exists |\n889\t| `sim` | Node, `game.advance` | Damage, crits, status, resources, cooldowns, XP curve, drops, salvage, craft, save round-trip and migration. **Coverage:** every skill x every Tone casts, costs, and hurts a dummy; every monster spawns, attacks, dies; every affix fires; every boss through every phase with scripted damage; with `draw: true` so draw errors land in `game.errors`. **Determinism:** the same seed and inputs give the same sim hash twice |\n890\t| `play` | Node | **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** the bot, driven by the quest data, from New Hero through the Prologue, all chapters, the ending, then a Vigil to its results screen, using all shops once, with cheats for speed (god mode, damage up). Asserts each quest flag in order and no errors. **Watchdog:** no progress in 120 game-seconds fails it. **Balance runs** (a separate flag, slower): no cheats, per zone, the bot must survive within a death budget. Run per hero |\n891\t| `browser` | Playwright, 1 browser | The single file from `file://`: no console errors, no external requests. Title appears. **Attract** begins at 10 s (±1), covers its vignettes, exits on each input kind, loops, touches no save. **Pad stub:** plays a fight, opens every panel, all reachable. **Mouse:** hover moves focus, click picks. **Prompts** follow the device, and change to A B X Y on the setting. **Touch profile:** notice and Settings button visible, attract runs. Pause menu reaches Dev Mode; every slider changes its value live, Reset restores it. Standard menus are TV-sized. **Audio:** music default is .1 and a render shows music, sfx and voice all non-silent, voice profiles differ in pitch, the Hush cuts highs |\n892\t| `hub` | Playwright, local server | The harness with `window.__hubCheck.pass` true and `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` for **all of** these, F being your built file: `?game=F&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Copy the built file beside the harness (same origin). **Plus your own:** two frames play for a minute: foe counts match, hero positions agree within tolerance, a kill on one shows on the other, personal loot stays personal, time-up finishes. Outside a session, the same file runs normally |\n893\t\n894\t**Other browsers:** smoke the final file once each in Firefox and WebKit: it loads, plays, and the TV menu scale holds.\n895\t\n896\t**A fast fake hub for `sim`:** two `world`s in one Node process, joined by a queue with latency and loss, catch most sync bugs in seconds, before the harness.\n897\t\n898\t**The bot is core infrastructure.** One bot drives followers, the attract mode and the playthrough. It picks targets, rolls out of telegraphs, uses skills by their tags, drinks, loots, equips upgrades, follows `quest.current().target`. Build it in the first milestone. Emberdeep's `93-autopilot.js` is a good reference.\n899\t\n900\t**`game.debug.snapshot()`** returns `{ scene, zone, quest, heroes, foes, attract, session, device, tuned }`. Every test and `tools/check.mjs` read it.\n901\t\n902\t**Screenshots only for what a script can't check** (`node tools/check.mjs game/index.html --size 1920x1080`): the look of each zone, filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs`) of each hero's main attacks, each boss phase, and the title. Act on `tools/check.mjs`'s look notes.\n903\t\n904\t---\n905\t\n906\t## 19. Order of work and cut order\n907\t\n908\tWork in this order. Each milestone has an exit test. Commit to the order: the multiplayer and test tools come before content because they are impossible to retrofit.\n909\t\n910\t| # | Milestone | Done when |\n911\t|---|---|---|\n912\t| 0 | **Setup.** Title picked per TASK.md. Handoff, hub files, build, test runner, file layout, one zone with a hero on screen in the single file | `tools/test.mjs` runs; the file opens from `file://` |\n913\t| 1 | **The first five minutes feel great.** World, hero (the Ringer), input for pad, keyboard and mouse, aim, two monsters, strike recipe, corpses launching, breakables, loot drop, basic HUD, basic sfx, the bot | Filmstrip of a swing looks right. Bot kills 30 foes headless. **Spend real time here; everything rests on it** |\n914\t| 2 | **Several heroes, couch co-op.** Drop-in, `cam.frame`, shared zone, personal loot | Two stubbed pads play together in the browser |\n915\t| 3 | **AI Hub round.** `net`, card, a basic Vigil map, finish, leave, server copy | All four harness scenarios pass. Keep them passing from now on |\n916\t| 4 | **The RPG layer.** XP, skills and Tones for the Ringer, Vows, the panel kit, Inventory and compare, Skills, services (Forge, Pawn), saves | Sim tests pass; panels navigable by all devices |\n917\t| 5 | **Front end and tools.** Title, Muster, attract (with the content so far), Dev Mode, Gallery, About, touch-only, TV menu scale, music default | Browser suite passes |\n918\t| 6 | **Chapter I complete.** Prologue, Knellwick, Acre, Nave, Undercroft, Beadle; all its monsters, elites, events, traps, story | Scripted playthrough runs it |\n919\t| 7 | **The other three heroes,** followers | Coverage test passes for each |\n920\t| 8 | **Chapters II and III, the ending, the Long Vigil in full** | Scripted playthrough finishes the game |\n921\t| 9 | **Audio pass.** The synth, score, voices, the Hush, all sfx | Audio checks pass; listen by render levels |\n922\t| 10 | **Everything else in the tour:** Relics, sets, gems, Lantern, Chandlery, Greater Vigil, Verses, Lambing Fields | Data lint counts met |\n923\t| 11 | **Polish and balance.** Bot balance runs, screenshots at 1080p against the Look target, every attract vignette, writing pass | All suites green; final bundle |\n924\t| 12 | **Paperwork and cleanup.** About screen, exit interview, chat reply. Delete `_repo` (150 MB, and anyone can fetch it again) | File parses; no TODOs or stubs in the build |\n925\t\n926\t### Cut order\n927\tIf budget runs out, cut from the top of this list. **Cut means gone:** no menu item, tip or code path left pointing at it. TASK.md allows no stubs. Say what you cut on the About screen and in your reply.\n928\t1. The Lambing Fields.\n929\t2. Greater Vigil and its table, then Verses.\n930\t3. Quillon's Lantern.\n931\t4. Vestment sets.\n932\t5. Blind Reliquary and Re-dip.\n933\t6. Mocap clips and GPU lighting.\n934\t7. The Scaffold of Heaven (the Stair leads straight to the Chamber).\n935\t8. Side crypts, The Sermon, lore page count down to 6.\n936\t9. The Bellworks' sluice beats (it stays a zone).\n937\t10. Relic count down to 12.\n938\t11. The Sexton, then the Lamplighter. Seats 2 and 3 repeat heroes in a recolored palette. Never fewer than two heroes. Followers stay.\n939\t\n940\t**Never cut, whatever happens:** the strike recipe; three chapter bosses and the story through its ending (a shortened Chapter II is fine); loot with Relics; six slots with Tones; the town and services basics; the Long Vigil basics (the hub round needs it); attract mode; Dev Mode with sliders and reset; both hub and couch multiplayer; pad, keyboard and mouse with live prompts and glyph setting; touch-only notice; all audio in code with gibberish voices and music at 10%; About/Credits; the single file; the one test command and scripted playthrough.\n941\t\n942\t---\n943\t\n944\t## 20. Coverage checklist (TASK.md to this plan)\n945\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"0cd0f2d1-5a08-460e-92e6-1fc0b864c8d0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:47.991Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 14. Attract mode\n\n**Trigger:** 10 seconds with no input on any front-end canvas screen (Title, Muster, Load). Not while a Settings, Controls or About screen is open; the player is reading there.\n**Exit:** any input: key, mouse move or click, wheel, pad button, stick past its dead zone. Back to the title with a short fade. Use your own listener set plus a poll of `navigator.getGamepads()`, as `input.anyPressed()` doesn't see sticks or mouse moves.\n**Touch-only:** it runs behind the restyled notice, and taps don't stop it (section 9).\n\n**What it is:** a looping tour played live by the bot, with cheats freely on (god mode, infinite resources, spawns, teleports). It uses a throwaway world and never touches saves. The director runs a list of vignettes of about 25 seconds, and the goal is to show as much of the game as possible:\n1. Knellwick: the party of four walks past the services, a refugee waves, the dog is petted.\n2. Potter's Acre: graves erupt, Toll the Hour kills thirty. A Requiem counter.\n3. The Nave: stained-glass light, pews smashed, Champions, a chandelier trap.\n4. Forced Relic drop: the beam, a pickup, a flash of the Inventory panel, the rig changing.\n5. Skills panel flash: a Tone swapped, the skill recast.\n6. Beadle Crake: a phase change and his death.\n7. The Salt March and Bellworks, Iven's Long Note, Wren's False Dawn, Maud's Potter's Field.\n8. Regent Sallow unfolding.\n9. Scaffold: the Great Toll rolling past.\n10. The Angelus's Toll, then the Long Vigil Reckoning filling.\n11. Title splash, controls, co-op line. Loop.\n\nA corner overlay shows the logo and `PRESS ANY BUTTON`. Browsers won't play sound before the first gesture, so attract is silent until then. Vignettes are data in `game/src/data/attract.js`, each `{ zone, heroes, setup, seconds, script }`, so a designer can reorder them.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Dev mode and designer tools\n\n### Dev Mode (pause menu item, hidden in sessions)\nA canvas panel with tabs, fully usable by pad, keyboard and mouse, at the same text sizes as the game. A small `DEV` marker shows while anything is on; `TUNED` while any slider differs from default.\n\n- **Cheats:** god mode, one-hit kills, infinite resource, no cooldowns, no-clip, freeze AI, reveal map, time scale (.1 to 3), pause and step one frame, restore life.\n- **Spawn:** any monster, count, elite tier, chosen affixes; any boss, from any phase; clear enemies; any item by slot, rarity, level; Relic or set piece by name; gold, materials, levels, XP; all skills and Tones.\n- **Travel:** any zone, any quest step (sets the flags), any chapter card, Vigil at tier N, the ending, the Lambing Fields, the Gallery, run the attract, autopilot on and off.\n- **Balance:** the live sliders below, each applied at once, with Reset per slider, per group and all. Saved in `E.store`. A Copy button puts the changed values as JSON on the clipboard and in the console, so a balance pass can become the new defaults.\n- **Overlays:** hitboxes, AI state above each monster, flow field, spawn points, network stats (RTT, messages/s, bytes), frame timing.\n\n**Sliders (default, range).** The most important variables, read through `TUNE.x` at the moment of use:\n\n| Group | Sliders |\n|---|---|\n| Hero | Damage x (1, .25-4), Life x (1, .25-4), Move speed x (1, .5-2), Attack speed x (1, .5-2), Cooldowns x (1, 0-2), Resource gain x (1, .25-4), Evade recharge s (5, 1-12), Potion cooldown s (20, 2-60), Votive chance (.14, 0-1) |\n| Monsters | Life x (1, .25-6), Damage x (1, .25-6), Speed x (1, .5-2), Density x (1, .25-4), Elite frequency x (1, 0-4), Telegraph time x (1, .5-2), Co-op life per hero (.75, 0-2) |\n| Rewards | XP x (1, 0-10), Pennies x (1, 0-10), Item drops x (1, 0-10), Relic chance x (1, 0-50), Vigil fill x (1, .25-4) |\n| Feel | Hit-stop x (1, 0-3), Knockback and launch x (1, 0-3), Screen shake x (1, 0-3), Aim assist x (1, 0-2), Requiem window s (1.6, .5-4) |\n\n### The Gallery (from Dev Mode, deep link `#gallery`)\nPlays every skill and Tone on dummies, every monster and affix walking in, attacking and dying, every boss pattern. A reel for eyes, and a test target for filmstrips and the data-coverage test.\n\n### So the rest could be built with designer tools\nTASK.md wants the infrastructure for a full game. That means:\n- **All content is data** in `game/src/data/*.js`, one registry per kind, validated by the lint. Adding a monster, skill, Relic, zone, event, quest or line needs no engine change.\n- **Levels** are ASCII with a legend, generators named by data, set dressing as `[id, across, forward]` scenes.\n- **Deep links:** `#zone/<id>`, `#boss/<id>/<phase>`, `#vigil/<tier>`, `#gallery/<kind>/<id>`, `#attract`, `#about`, and `?seed=`.\n- **`game/CONTENT.md`,** at most two pages: how to add each kind, with one worked example. Keep it true.\n- **Saves are versioned,** `game.saves` with `version` and `migrate`.\n\n---\n\n## 16. About/Credits and the paperwork\n\n**About/Credits screen** (title and pause, deep link `#about`): paged, L1 and R1 or arrows or a click to turn, readable at 10 feet. Contents exactly as TASK.md lists: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, and Credits: the engine (MIT, Michael Crosato), Emberdeep parts used, asset store sources by name (Kenney, KayKit and so on, each CC0), mocap sources if used, session client. Usage reads \"added on import\", as TASK.md says. \"Unknown\" for what you can't confirm.\n\n**One source:** keep all this in `game/src/data/about.js` and generate TASK.md's exit interview file from the same data in the build, so the screen and the file can't disagree. Check that the file parses.\n\n**Exit interview's `aiHub` block, suggested:** type `Game`, genre `RPG`, source `Diablo 3`, series `Diablo`, players `1–4`, tags from `co-op`, `fantasy`, `pixel art`, `boss fights`, `story`, plus `isometric`. Controls in one line. Tagline and description in the game's voice, without the source's names.\n\nRemember the chat reply too: TASK.md requires the same information there.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Tech plan\n\n### Setup (first half hour)\n```sh\n# in your dev folder\ngit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge _repo     # for Emberdeep parts, mocap; never bundled whole\ncp -r _repo/dist/handoff/. .                                              # the handoff: its layout is the dev folder's layout\nnpm install                                                               # Playwright 1.63.0. Never `playwright install` here\nmkdir hub && cd hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do\n  curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done; cd ..\n```\nRead `API.md` whole, then `docs/ASSETS.md`, and search `API-INDEX.md` and `AI_GUIDE.md` for names. Read `hub/README.md` whole (the protocol); `hub/arena.html` is a working shared world. Stack: plain JavaScript on the full engine (`my-3d2dge.js`, all modules included). No other libraries, no CDN needed.\n\n### Files\n```\nmy-3d2dge.js, API.md, tools/, kits/, ...   the handoff\ngame/index.html                            dev page (loads the built game.js)\ngame/src/00-core.js ... 90-start.js        joined in name order into one IIFE (Emberdeep's pattern)\ngame/src/data/*.js                         all content\ngame/CONTENT.md                            designer's how-to\ntools/build.mjs                            join; inline session.js, engine, asset set, game into the single HTML\ntools/test.mjs                             the one test command (section 18)\n```\nSuggested parts of `game/src`: `core` (game, `def`, BUS, RNG streams, TUNE), `input` (presets, prompts, aim), `world` (world, step), `combat` (damage, statuses, fx verbs), `hero`, `skills`, `ai` (monsters, bot), `loot`, `progress` (XP, Vows, quests, saves), `render-*` (rigs, gear, themes, props, decals, fx, lights), `ui-*` (panel kit, HUD, each screen), `net`, `audio-*` (synth, music, sfx, voice), `attract`, `dev`, `about`.\n\n**The single file:** `<meta charset>`, then `session.js` as the first script, unmodified; hub tags; `<title>`; styles; `<body>` with the boot splash markup (copy it from the template's `game/index.html`), canvas, engine, asset set, game. Write every `</script` inside inlined scripts as `<\\/script`. It must run from `file://` with no network.\n\n### Architecture rules (these prevent the expensive rewrites)\n1. **`world` holds everything; no hero singleton.** `world.heroes[]`, `world.me` (null on a server copy), `world.foes`, `world.fx`, `world.drops`, `world.map`, `world.authority`.\n2. **Heroes read an abstract input,** `{ moveDir, aim, pressed(slot), ... }`, built from a device (`game.players[i]`), the bot, or the network. Nothing in hero code touches `game.input`.\n3. **The simulation never reads rigs or draws.** Visuals read the sim. Spawn projectiles from fixed offsets and let the visual start at the hand. So a server copy and headless runs can skip rig updates entirely.\n4. **One damage pipeline:** `dealDamage(target, hit)`, only when `world.authority`.\n5. **Every effect is a verb with JSON params:** `fx('cone' | 'bolt' | 'nova' | 'area' | 'telegraph' | 'chain' | 'beam' | 'wave' | 'pull' | 'leap' | 'summon' | 'lob', params)`. Skills, monsters, bosses, traps and Relics all use them. See `FX.*` in Emberdeep's `10-combat.js`.\n6. **Randomness from named streams** (`E.rng(seed)`; in a session `AIHub.rng(label)`): `map`, `loot`, `ai`, cosmetics apart. `Math.random` never affects the sim: in shared world it isn't seeded, and rigs call it for blinks.\n7. **All content through `def(kind, id, spec)`,** referred to by id. Listeners on a `BUS` (`hit`, `kill`, `skill`, `evade`, `pickup`, `step`) let Relics and tips attach without touching combat.\n8. **Knobs:** every balance number reads `TUNE.x` when used.\n9. **UI layouts and rects are computed in `update`,** drawn in `draw`, so mouse hits and tests work headless. Input is read only in `update`.\n10. **One panel kit:** focusable rects with automatic directional navigation (nearest rect in the pressed direction), `input.repeat`, hover sets focus, click picks, a prompt bar at the bottom that follows the last device.\n\n**Data shapes, to set the pattern:**\n```js\ndef('skill', 'knell', { hero: 'ringer', name: 'Knell', unlock: 3, cost: { peal: 30 }, cd: 0, icon: 'bellSlam', tags: ['toll'],\n  move: 'overhead', wind: .22, active: .1, recover: .3,\n  verbs: [{ fx: 'cone', on: 'active', range: 40, half: .9, dmg: 3.2, el: 'phys', kb: 120 }],\n  tones: { deep: { name: 'Deep', text: 'A ring drags foes in before it lands.', add: [{ fx: 'pull', on: 'wind', r: 70, power: 140 }] } /* ... */ } });\ndef('monster', 'bellWight', { name: 'Bell-Wight', body: { rig: 'humanoid', o: { hunch: .35, size: 1.15, outfit: 'tunic' } }, ai: 'shamble', speed: 32,\n  life: 1, dmg: 1, xp: 1, attacks: [{ move: 'claw', wind: .35, range: 14, dmg: 1 }], enter: 'graveRise', death: 'fling', sound: { idle: 'smallBell' }, tags: ['undead'] });\ndef('zone', 'pottersAcre', { name: \"Potter's Acre\", chapter: 1, level: [1, 4], layout: 'yard', size: [100, 100], theme: 'graveyard',\n  pool: { bellWight: 10, boneDigger: 4, carrionRook: 2 }, elites: [1, 2], events: ['unquietRow'], shrines: 1, music: 'acre', weather: { kind: 'rain', amount: .4 }, lychgate: true });\n```\n\n### Game creation (the parts verified or that trap people)\n```js\nconst session = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [480, 270], expand: true, view: 'iso', bg: '#05040a', touch: 'never',\n  input: PLAY_PRESET, live: session, autoPause: !session,\n  menu: { items: session ? [] : PAUSE_ITEMS, quit: session ? false : 'title', controls: CONTROL_NAMES,\n    settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox (A B X Y)']] }, /* yours */] } });\n```\n\n### The parts bin: Emberdeep\n`_repo/src/emberdeep/` is a whole Diablo-style game on this engine, MIT, same owner. **Do not fork it.** It assumes one hero (`ED.hero` appears 354 times ✔), its menus are mouse-first and replace the standard ones, its UI is small and dense, and it's a different game. Instead, read `DESIGN.md`, copy algorithms and rigs out, rename everything to this game's terms, and credit it.\n\n| You need | Look at |\n|---|---|\n| Damage, knockback, FX verbs | `10-combat.js`, `05-elements.js` |\n| Hero actions, roll, IK potion, wounded hunch, gear look | `20-hero.js` |\n| Skill runtime and worked skills | `25-skills-core.js`, `26-skills-melee.js`, `27-skills-spells.js` |\n| Monster AI, affixes, worked monsters | `30-monsters-core.js`, `31-monsters.js` |\n| Crawler, serpent, eye rigs | `33-beasts.js` |\n| Boss runtime and pattern library | `35-bosses-core.js`, `36-bosses.js` |\n| Item generation, labels, panels | `40-loot-core.js`, `42-inventory.js` |\n| Level building, floors, themes, dressing | `50-levels-core.js`, `51-themes.js`, `52-layouts.js`, `53-scenes.js` |\n| NPCs and a town | `55-town-core.js`, `56-town.js` |\n| Dev tools, tuning, gallery, autopilot, rumble | `62-developer.js`, `01-tune.js`, `92-gallery.js`, `93-autopilot.js`, `97-rumble.js` |\n\n**`kits/adventure.js`** is the kit the API card names for this genre: read how it sets scenes, lights and GPU fallback. `kits/brawler.js` shows drop-in players. `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs` show the Node stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`). Then start from the rules above rather than bending a kit.\n\n### Engine changes to expect (you may change anything; keep a list for the feedback)\n- **Weapons and hats are closed lists** ✔ (constructor at about line 4073, `['sword', 'gun', 'staff']`; drawing at about lines 4649-4656 and 4729-4736). Add a registry: `E.Humanoid.WEAPONS[id] = { len, draw(g, ctx) }`, accept those ids, draw them there, set `bladeLen`. A dozen builders did the same. Same for hats, plus a draw hook for attachments (rope wraps, blindfold, mask, wings).\n- **Pan and loops** on sound aren't built in: your own synth handles them.\n\n### Traps\n- `game.go` clears timers, tweens, particles and weather (`{ keep: true }` outlives it). Tests set `game.fadeTime = 0`.\n- A frame past 50 ms gives up its time. A browser test waits on state, never the clock.\n- `E.font` text with characters it lacks prints `?`. Colors must be `#rrggbb`; a bad one draws magenta.\n- `input.tap` is no device, so prompts don't change in tests. `input.feed('move', x, y)` plays a pointer.\n- `r.pick` needs a drawn frame: hover tests need the browser or `draw: true`.\n- A map over 128x128 bakes floors in chunks automatically.\n- Weather ends with the scene: set it in `enter`.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Testing\n\n**One command:** `node tools/test.mjs [data|sim|play|browser|hub]` (no argument: all). It prints only failures and a final one-line count. Rerun a suite only after changing what it covers. Don't use subagents or workflows to review, debate or judge. Use the stand-ins TASK.md lists: a `navigator.getGamepads` stub with a standard-mapping pad, Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, `OfflineAudioContext` and `AnalyserNode`, two browser pages for multiplayer. One or two browsers at a time, closed when done. No server unless needed; when needed, `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page is yours, stop your own PID only.\n\n| Suite | Runs in | Checks |\n|---|---|---|\n| `data` | Node | Every registry's required fields; every referenced id exists; every skill has 3 Tones with text; 24 Relics; every string uses only font characters and fits its box (`E.font.width`); the banned-word list; every quest step's target exists |\n| `sim` | Node, `game.advance` | Damage, crits, status, resources, cooldowns, XP curve, drops, salvage, craft, save round-trip and migration. **Coverage:** every skill x every Tone casts, costs, and hurts a dummy; every monster spawns, attacks, dies; every affix fires; every boss through every phase with scripted damage; with `draw: true` so draw errors land in `game.errors`. **Determinism:** the same seed and inputs give the same sim hash twice |\n| `play` | Node | **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** the bot, driven by the quest data, from New Hero through the Prologue, all chapters, the ending, then a Vigil to its results screen, using all shops once, with cheats for speed (god mode, damage up). Asserts each quest flag in order and no errors. **Watchdog:** no progress in 120 game-seconds fails it. **Balance runs** (a separate flag, slower): no cheats, per zone, the bot must survive within a death budget. Run per hero |\n| `browser` | Playwright, 1 browser | The single file from `file://`: no console errors, no external requests. Title appears. **Attract** begins at 10 s (±1), covers its vignettes, exits on each input kind, loops, touches no save. **Pad stub:** plays a fight, opens every panel, all reachable. **Mouse:** hover moves focus, click picks. **Prompts** follow the device, and change to A B X Y on the setting. **Touch profile:** notice and Settings button visible, attract runs. Pause menu reaches Dev Mode; every slider changes its value live, Reset restores it. Standard menus are TV-sized. **Audio:** music default is .1 and a render shows music, sfx and voice all non-silent, voice profiles differ in pitch, the Hush cuts highs |\n| `hub` | Playwright, local server | The harness with `window.__hubCheck.pass` true and `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` for **all of** these, F being your built file: `?game=F&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Copy the built file beside the harness (same origin). **Plus your own:** two frames play for a minute: foe counts match, hero positions agree within tolerance, a kill on one shows on the other, personal loot stays personal, time-up finishes. Outside a session, the same file runs normally |\n\n**Other browsers:** smoke the final file once each in Firefox and WebKit: it loads, plays, and the TV menu scale holds.\n\n**A fast fake hub for `sim`:** two `world`s in one Node process, joined by a queue with latency and loss, catch most sync bugs in seconds, before the harness.\n\n**The bot is core infrastructure.** One bot drives followers, the attract mode and the playthrough. It picks targets, rolls out of telegraphs, uses skills by their tags, drinks, loots, equips upgrades, follows `quest.current().target`. Build it in the first milestone. Emberdeep's `93-autopilot.js` is a good reference.\n\n**`game.debug.snapshot()`** returns `{ scene, zone, quest, heroes, foes, attract, session, device, tuned }`. Every test and `tools/check.mjs` read it.\n\n**Screenshots only for what a script can't check** (`node tools/check.mjs game/index.html --size 1920x1080`): the look of each zone, filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs`) of each hero's main attacks, each boss phase, and the title. Act on `tools/check.mjs`'s look notes.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Order of work and cut order\n\nWork in this order. Each milestone has an exit test. Commit to the order: the multiplayer and test tools come before content because they are impossible to retrofit.\n\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | **Setup.** Title picked per TASK.md. Handoff, hub files, build, test runner, file layout, one zone with a hero on screen in the single file | `tools/test.mjs` runs; the file opens from `file://` |\n| 1 | **The first five minutes feel great.** World, hero (the Ringer), input for pad, keyboard and mouse, aim, two monsters, strike recipe, corpses launching, breakables, loot drop, basic HUD, basic sfx, the bot | Filmstrip of a swing looks right. Bot kills 30 foes headless. **Spend real time here; everything rests on it** |\n| 2 | **Several heroes, couch co-op.** Drop-in, `cam.frame`, shared zone, personal loot | Two stubbed pads play together in the browser |\n| 3 | **AI Hub round.** `net`, card, a basic Vigil map, finish, leave, server copy | All four harness scenarios pass. Keep them passing from now on |\n| 4 | **The RPG layer.** XP, skills and Tones for the Ringer, Vows, the panel kit, Inventory and compare, Skills, services (Forge, Pawn), saves | Sim tests pass; panels navigable by all devices |\n| 5 | **Front end and tools.** Title, Muster, attract (with the content so far), Dev Mode, Gallery, About, touch-only, TV menu scale, music default | Browser suite passes |\n| 6 | **Chapter I complete.** Prologue, Knellwick, Acre, Nave, Undercroft, Beadle; all its monsters, elites, events, traps, story | Scripted playthrough runs it |\n| 7 | **The other three heroes,** followers | Coverage test passes for each |\n| 8 | **Chapters II and III, the ending, the Long Vigil in full** | Scripted playthrough finishes the game |\n| 9 | **Audio pass.** The synth, score, voices, the Hush, all sfx | Audio checks pass; listen by render levels |\n| 10 | **Everything else in the tour:** Relics, sets, gems, Lantern, Chandlery, Greater Vigil, Verses, Lambing Fields | Data lint counts met |\n| 11 | **Polish and balance.** Bot balance runs, screenshots at 1080p against the Look target, every attract vignette, writing pass | All suites green; final bundle |\n| 12 | **Paperwork and cleanup.** About screen, exit interview, chat reply. Delete `_repo` (150 MB, and anyone can fetch it again) | File parses; no TODOs or stubs in the build |\n\n### Cut order\nIf budget runs out, cut from the top of this list. **Cut means gone:** no menu item, tip or code path left pointing at it. TASK.md allows no stubs. Say what you cut on the About screen and in your reply.\n1. The Lambing Fields.\n2. Greater Vigil and its table, then Verses.\n3. Quillon's Lantern.\n4. Vestment sets.\n5. Blind Reliquary and Re-dip.\n6. Mocap clips and GPU lighting.\n7. The Scaffold of Heaven (the Stair leads straight to the Chamber).\n8. Side crypts, The Sermon, lore page count down to 6.\n9. The Bellworks' sluice beats (it stays a zone).\n10. Relic count down to 12.\n11. The Sexton, then the Lamplighter. Seats 2 and 3 repeat heroes in a recolored palette. Never fewer than two heroes. Followers stay.\n\n**Never cut, whatever happens:** the strike recipe; three chapter bosses and the story through its ending (a shortened Chapter II is fine); loot with Relics; six slots with Tones; the town and services basics; the Long Vigil basics (the hub round needs it); attract mode; Dev Mode with sliders and reset; both hub and couch multiplayer; pad, keyboard and mouse with live prompts and glyph setting; touch-only notice; all audio in code with gibberish voices and music at 10%; About/Credits; the single file; the one test command and scripted playthrough.\n\n---\n\n## 20. Coverage checklist (TASK.md to this plan)\n","numLines":225,"startLine":721,"totalLines":973}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VWKSw2dpzTjbiLCDWiGNkE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
