{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBWjFDiMorU8nBTwBVf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `PLAN.md` (about 16,000 words), and its last section maps each TASK.md requirement to the part of the plan that covers it. The prompt review is in `planner-exit-interview.json`, with all four answers, and it parses as valid JSON. As STAGE.md asked, the plan leaves the title to each builder, doesn't use TASK.md's file or folder names, and gives paths relative to the dev folder.\n\n**The game:** an isometric action RPG for 1–4 players, in an original world built around bells. The bells hold back a hungry silence called the Hush. The Great Bell falls through an abbey roof, and four parish nobodies (a bell-ringer, a cantor, a lamplighter and a sexton) find their names missing from the Book of the Dead, so death can't keep them. They carry the talking severed head of a beheaded abbess, and the story's ending is hers. Only genre, mechanics and tone come from Diablo 3; a test in the plan fails if the source's names appear in the game.\n\n**What the plan specifies:**\n- **Content:** four heroes with 8 skills and 3 variants each, 20 monsters, 12 elite modifiers, 3 bosses, 12 zones and an endless endgame mode.\n- **Systems:** loot, controls, screens, art, animation and code-only audio, including gibberish voices.\n- **Build path:** the file layout, 12 test-gated milestones, and an order for cutting features if a builder runs short, plus a list of what must never be cut.\n\n**Checked on this machine:** I marked about 20 facts with ✔ so builders can trust them. Most came from running them against engine v0.88.0:\n- Music defaults to 10%.\n- PlayStation and Xbox button prompts work.\n- 480×270 scales cleanly to a TV.\n- The engine's pause menu scales to TV size with one line of CSS.\n- The touch-only notice can be restyled so the attract mode shows behind it.\n- The D-pad can be freed for shortcuts during play.\n\nThe rest came from reading the code, such as the hub's message limits and what its test harness does.\n\n**Judgment calls to look over:**\n- **Multiplayer \"on its own\":** the hub docs don't define this, so I planned couch co-op on one screen, with online play only through hub sessions.\n- **Attract mode:** I excluded Settings and About from its 10-second idle rule, so it won't interrupt someone reading.\n- **Emberdeep:** the plan tells builders to borrow code from the engine's Diablo-style game rather than fork it, because it's built around a single hero.\n- **Plan length:** I found a repo note saying builders of mixed ability work from these plans, which is why the cut order exists. I can't test from here how well weaker builders handle a plan this long. The review raises this and suggests stating the audience and a target length in the prompt.\n\nI deleted my scratch clones, so the folder now holds only `STAGE.md`, `TASK.md` and the two new files. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":451869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751},"output_tokens":716,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"240bf137-8c31-4d30-9d14-91b20fbb9fdc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:52:52.025Z","request_id":"req_011CgjBWixc9Ru3oyJkSgAhE"}
