{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBwSdnE9wvrSbbbm5ay","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S3JvHcyKH5vU835q7hcq8S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, sys\np = 'PLAN.md'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new, n=1):\n    global s\n    if s.count(old) != n: sys.exit(f'expected {n}: ' + old[:70])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\nrep(\"This plan holds only the form on purpose: the literal string is unique to each build, so any one build's would be wrong for all the others. \"\n    \"That one string is both the dev subfolder's name and, with `.html` added, the game's file name. Copy it character for character, and keep it in one constant that `tools/build.mjs` reads. \",\n    \"This plan holds only the form on purpose: the literal string is unique to each build, so any one build's would be wrong for all the others. To print your exact string, run this in the folder that holds your TASK.md, before you make the dev subfolder:\\n\"\n    \"```sh\\n\"\n    \"grep -o '\\\\[GameTitle[^]]*\\\\]' TASK.md | head -1\\n\"\n    \"```\\n\"\n    \"That one string is both the dev subfolder's name and, with `.html` added, the game's file name. Fill in your title and the source, copy the rest character for character, and keep the result in one constant that `tools/build.mjs` reads, so the folder and the file can't disagree. \")\nrep(\"16 (the name's form; the literal string is in your TASK.md), 17 |\", \"16 (the name's form, and a command that prints your exact string), 17 |\", 2)\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\n\nf = 'planner-exit-interview.json'\nd = json.load(open(f, encoding='utf-8'))\nextra = \" 7) Write STAGE.md's exception into the goal's done-when line, for example 'everything TASK.md asks for, apart from its file and folder names'. As written, the automatic check kept reading 'covers everything' as requiring the literal name that STAGE.md forbids, and the two could not both be satisfied that way.\"\nassert d[3]['question'] == 'What would you change in this prompt?'\nd[3]['answer'] += extra\njson.dump(d, open(f, 'w', encoding='utf-8'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\nopen(f, 'a', encoding='utf-8').write('\\n')\nPY\necho '--- the plan'\"'\"'s command, run for real on this TASK.md (output is this run'\"'\"'s name, printed here and not stored in the plan):'\nsed -n \"/^grep -o/p\" PLAN.md > /dev/null; cmd=$(grep -m1 \"^grep -o\" PLAN.md); echo \"\\$ $cmd\"; eval \"$cmd\"\necho '--- literal name in PLAN.md? (count must be 0)'; lit=$(eval \"$cmd\"); grep -cF \"$lit\" PLAN.md\necho '--- appearances of that name in TASK.md'; grep -cF \"$lit\" TASK.md\npython3 -c \"import json; print(len(json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json'))), 'interview answers, valid JSON')\"","description":"Add name-printing command to plan and test it on TASK.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":839,"cache_read_input_tokens":487950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":839},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"fa60e145-fc24-4760-9c5d-889f621016c7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:59:00.309Z","request_id":"req_011CgjBwSKvScC5JGQWbpYjT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01S3JvHcyKH5vU835q7hcq8S":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211938__x30f875/work && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, sys\np = 'PLAN.md'\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new, n=1):\n    global s\n    if s.count(old) != n: sys.exit(f'expected {n}: ' + old[:70])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\nrep(\"This plan holds only the form on purpose: the liter