{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DWcH7cbSymb3muMh6Nz2oF","type":"tool_result","content":"e688de41 Michael 2026-11-04\nPlans leave out TASK.md's file names: each builder's TASK.md has its own (#28)\n\nThe plan stage (plan-v2, never run, so it keeps its name) now says: \"Leave out TASK.md's file and folder names too, since each builder's TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\" 23 of 25 v6 plans copied the planner's own run names into PLAN.md (100 times), wrong for every builder; 67 builders said translating them cost time. Module paths inside the dev folder (21 of 25 plans) \n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n--- files changed\n audit.json         | 15 ++++++++-------\n dashboard.html     |  2 +-\n matrix.config.json |  2 +-\n 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n--- lines about file names, in the change itself\n10:-   \"title\": \"Keep file names out of PLAN.md (PLAN-2)\",\n11:-   \"detail\": \"Optional. The planner copies its own file names into the plan, and every builder has to translate them. It cost time but caused no wrong files. Now that builders draw their own titles, the plan's names will match even less. A line in the plan stage would do it: \\\"Write paths relative to the dev folder; each builder takes its own file names from its TASK.md.\\\"\"\n22:    \"title\": \"Plans hard-code the plan run's own file names, and 67 builders had to translate them\",\n23:    \"found\": \"The planner's TASK.md names its files after the plan run (`…-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728`), and 23 of 25 plans copy those names into PLAN.md, 91 times in all. Each builder's TASK.md has its own names. \\\"TASK.md wins\\\" settled it, and no build shipped under the planner's names, but 67 builders said it cost time: opus-xhigh baseball wrote that \\\"every path in the plan had to be translated\\\".\",\n24:-   \"did\": \"Left for you: tell the planner not to write file names (Your call).\",\n25:+   \"did\": \"**Decided Nov 4 (you left it to me): keep them out.** The plan stage now adds: \\\"Leave out TASK.md's file and folder names too, since each builder's TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\\\"\\n\\n- **For:**\\n  - Every one of those names is wrong for every builder: the model, effort and start time differ, and now the title too, since builders draw their own.\\n  - 23 of 25 v6 plans had\n39:+   \"title\": \"Plans leave out TASK.md's file names\",\n40:+   \"detail\": \"The plan stage tells the planner its TASK.md's file and folder names are its own, so it writes paths relative to the dev folder instead (PLAN-2).\"\n54:+    text: 'You are the game director. TASK.md is the CEO\\'s brief. Write PLAN.md: the plan other AI agents will build the game from, without you. Leave the game\\'s title to them: each builder picks its own, as TASK.md says. Leave out TASK.md\\'s file and folder names too, since each builder\\'s TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\\n\\n'\n67:+      \"text\": \"You are the game director. TASK.md is the CEO's brief. Write PLAN.md: the plan other AI agents will build the game from, without you. Leave the game's title to them: each builder picks its own, as TASK.md says. Leave out TASK.md's file and folder names too, since each builder's TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\\n\\nThen review the prompt you were given (TASK.md and these i","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d255c30e-7719-4824-967e-28ca23bddd23","uuid":"c22f81d3-8f95-408a-8112-a712679a665b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:59:32.606Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"e688de41 Michael 2026-11-04\nPlans leave out TASK.md's file names: each builder's TASK.md has its own (#28)\n\nThe plan stage (plan-v2, never run, so it keeps its name) now says: \"Leave out TASK.md's file and folder names too, since each builder's TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\" 23 of 25 v6 plans copied the planner's own run names into PLAN.md (100 times), wrong for every builder; 67 builders said translating them cost time. Module paths inside the dev folder (21 of 25 plans) \n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n--- files changed\n audit.json         | 15 ++++++++-------\n dashboard.html     |  2 +-\n matrix.config.json |  2 +-\n 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n--- lines about file names, in the change itself\n10:-   \"title\": \"Keep file names out of PLAN.md (PLAN-2)\",\n11:-   \"detail\": \"Optional. The planner copies its own file names into the plan, and every builder has to translate them. It cost time but caused no wrong files. Now that builders draw their own titles, the plan's names will match even less. A line in the plan stage would do it: \\\"Write paths relative to the dev folder; each builder takes its own file names from its TASK.md.\\\"\"\n22:    \"title\": \"Plans hard-code the plan run's own file names, and 67 builders had to translate them\",\n23:    \"found\": \"The planner's TASK.md names its files after the plan run (`…-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728`), and 23 of 25 plans copy those names into PLAN.md, 91 times in all. Each builder's TASK.md has its own names. \\\"TASK.md wins\\\" settled it, and no build shipped under the planner's names, but 67 builders said it cost time: opus-xhigh baseball wrote that \\\"every path in the plan had to be translated\\\".\",\n24:-   \"did\": \"Left for you: tell the planner not to write file names (Your call).\",\n25:+   \"did\": \"**Decided Nov 4 (you left it to me): keep them out.** The plan stage now adds: \\\"Leave out TASK.md's file and folder names too, since each builder's TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\\\"\\n\\n- **For:**\\n  - Every one of those names is wrong for every builder: the model, effort and start time differ, and now the title too, since builders draw their own.\\n  - 23 of 25 v6 plans had\n39:+   \"title\": \"Plans leave out TASK.md's file names\",\n40:+   \"detail\": \"The plan stage tells the planner its TASK.md's file and folder names are its own, so it writes paths relative to the dev folder instead (PLAN-2).\"\n54:+    text: 'You are the game director. TASK.md is the CEO\\'s brief. Write PLAN.md: the plan other AI agents will build the game from, without you. Leave the game\\'s title to them: each builder picks its own, as TASK.md says. Leave out TASK.md\\'s file and folder names too, since each builder\\'s TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\\n\\n'\n67:+      \"text\": \"You are the game director. TASK.md is the CEO's brief. Write PLAN.md: the plan other AI agents will build the game from, without you. Leave the game's title to them: each builder picks its own, as TASK.md says. Leave out TASK.md's file and folder names too, since each builder's TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\\n\\nThen review the prompt you were given (TASK.md and these i","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DWcH7cbSymb3muMh6Nz2oF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
