{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjC32JDxfzfvH3FSqQdj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The omission is settled, so you don't need to decide anything and I'm withdrawing that request. `PLAN.md` is correct as it stands, and I changed nothing this round.\n\n**The evidence:** your repo already records this decision, in commit `e688de41`, \"Plans leave out TASK.md's file names\". `audit.json` lists it as item PLAN-2, \"Decided Nov 4 (you left it to me): keep them out\", and STAGE.md's sentence comes from that commit. It gives these reasons:\n- 23 of 25 earlier plans copied the planner's run names into PLAN.md, about 100 times.\n- Those names were wrong for every builder, because the model, effort, start time and title all differ.\n- 67 builders said translating them cost time.\n\n**What that means for the done-when line:** \"covers everything TASK.md asks for\" has to be read together with that decision. TASK.md requires each builder to use their own name, and the audit's original suggestion was \"each builder takes its own file names from its TASK.md\". The literal string in this run's TASK.md is exactly what that decision removed.\n\n**How the plan handles names:**\n- Every path is relative to the dev folder, so there's nothing to translate.\n- Section 16 gives the name's pattern with placeholders only, and none of this run's values.\n- It also gives a command that prints each builder's exact name from their own TASK.md. I tested it here, and it printed the exact name while `PLAN.md` holds no copies of it.\n\n**Final state:** `PLAN.md` covers every other TASK.md requirement, listed one by one in section 20, and `planner-exit-interview.json` holds all four answers as valid JSON. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2695,"cache_read_input_tokens":494763,"cache_creation":{"ephem